hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2401","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated: from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Ali ibn Mudrik, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir: Jarir narrated, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the sudden glance, and he said: Turn away your gaze."
"2402","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated (ha), and Yusuf al-Qadi, Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated; both said: Sufyan narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the sudden glance, and he commanded me to turn away my sight."
"2403","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Yazid ibn Zuray and Abd al-Warith narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the sudden glance, and he commanded me to turn away my sight."
"2404","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid informed us: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2405","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from his father, that Jarir asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the sudden glance, and he said: Turn away your sight."
"2406","Abu Husayn narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2407","Yusuf al-Qadi and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twisting the forelock of a horse between his fingers, and he said: Good is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: booty and reward."
"2408","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated (ha), and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon hearing and obeying, and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2409","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated (ha), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Mualla ibn Mahdi narrated; both said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses, good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and booty."
"2410","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Askari narrated to us: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2411","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Abd al-Warith narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2412","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, both said: Musaddad narrated: Abd al-Warith narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon hearing and obeying, and sincere advice to every Muslim. Whenever he bought or sold anything, he would say to its owner: Know that what I take from you is dearer to us than what we give you, so choose."
"2413","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid informed us: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2414","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us: Mualla ibn Asad narrated: Wuhayb narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2415","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated: from Isa ibn Ubayd, from Ghaylan ibn Abd Allah al-Amiri, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty revealed to me: whichever of these three lands you settle in, it is your land of migration: Madinah, or al-Bahrayn, or Qinnasrin."
"2416","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Khalid ibn Ziyad al-Zayyat narrated: Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir narrated to me: from Jarir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, he said to his Companions: Come with us to the people of Quba to greet them. He came to them and greeted them, and they welcomed him. Then he said: O people of Quba, bring me stones from this lava field. Many stones were gathered before him, and with him was a short spear of his. He marked their qiblah, took a stone, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed it. Then he said: O Abu Bakr, take a stone and place it beside my stone. Then he said: O Umar, take a stone and place it beside the stone of Abu Bakr. Then he turned and said: O Uthman, take a stone and place it beside the stone of Umar. Then he turned to the people at the end and said: Let each man place his stone wherever he likes along this line."
"2417","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj al-Askari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated: from Marwan ibn Salim, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad when he enters his house, poverty is kept away from the people of that house and the neighbors."
"2418","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated: Khalid ibn Amr al-Umawi narrated: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated: from Abu Zurah, from Jarir, he said: Whenever delegations came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would call them and boast of me to them."
"2419","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: I saw Jarir ibn Abd Allah urinate, then wipe over his leather socks. It was said to him, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do that. Ibrahim said: They used to hold that wiping was after the revelation of al-Maidah, because Jarir was among the last of them to embrace Islam."
"2420","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah (ha), and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: I saw Jarir ibn Abd Allah perform ablution from the mosque's water vessel and wipe over his leather socks. It was said to him about that, so he said: What prevents me, when I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"2421","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated: Zaidah narrated: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: Jarir urinated, performed ablution, and wiped over the leather socks. A man from among the people objected to that, so Jarir said: If I do it, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do this."
"2422","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Usamah narrated: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over his leather socks. Ibrahim said: Our companions used to admire the hadith of Jarir, saying: His Islam was after the revelation of al-Maidah."
"2423","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith: that Jarir urinated, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks. It was said to him, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"2424","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated: Shuabah narrated: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, that Jarir urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"2425","Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated: from Dawud al-Tai, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir: that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."
"2426","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjunani narrated: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated: from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: Jarir urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. I said to him: Do you do this after having urinated? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."
"2427","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated: Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: Jarir urinated, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"2428","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Abu Muawiyah narrated: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"2429","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Aban narrated to me: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated: al-Qasim ibn al-Walid narrated: from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day, concerning wiping over the leather socks."
"2430","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"2431","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us: Habib ibn Bishr narrated: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated: from Shuabah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, that he saw Jarir ibn Abd Allah urinate, wipe over the leather socks, and pray. He was asked about that, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over them."
"2432","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated: al-Hakam ibn Bashir narrated: from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Jarir: that he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. It was said to him, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping, so I wiped."
"2433","Salih ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Muqatil narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Wasiti narrated: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated: Shuabah narrated: from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, he said: Jarir urinated, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do the like of that."
"2434","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us: Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah narrated: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated: Shuabah narrated: from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ibrahim narrating from Hammam ibn al-Harith, that Jarir urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing the like of this."
"2435","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated: Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated: from Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: I heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah while he was addressing the people, and among what he would do was come to the pulpit until he stood upon it. I heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever institutes a good practice in Islam, he will have the like of the reward of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam, upon him will be the like of the burden of whoever acts upon it, in that nothing is diminished from their burdens."
"2436","Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Shibami narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us: from al-Amash, from Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter, and the freed captives of Quraysh and the freed slaves of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"2437","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Mamar informed us: from Qatadah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali, that a man from the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a bag of gold filling what is between his fingers, and said: This is in the path of Allah. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and gave. Then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and gave. Then the Muhajirun and the Ansar stood and gave. The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brightened until we saw the radiance in his cheek. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever institutes a righteous practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, he will have the like of their rewards without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, upon him will be the like of their burdens without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"2438","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Thalabah ibn Sawa narrated: my uncle Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated: from Qatadah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2439","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Yahya ibn Said narrated (ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Ali ibn Mushir narrated; both said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal al-Absi narrated: Jarir ibn Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant institutes a righteous practice that is acted upon after him except that he will have the like of the reward of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And no servant institutes an evil practice that is acted upon after him except that upon him will be the like of the burden of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their burdens. And some Bedouin people came and said: Your zakah collectors come to us and wrong us. He said: Please your zakah collectors."
"2440","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sahl narrated: Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated: al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to me: from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal al-Absi, from Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none who institutes a good practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him except that he will have the like of the reward of whoever acts upon it after him, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, except that upon him will be the like of the burdens of those who act upon it after him, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"2441","Ahmad ibn al-Jarud al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muawiyah al-Asbahani narrated: Husayn ibn Hafs narrated: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated: from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Hilal al-Absi, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no man who institutes a good practice in Islam, then he mentioned the like of it."
"2442","Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us: Salm ibn Junadah narrated: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated: from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Hilal, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2443","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Jarir narrated: from al-Amash, from Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid and Abu al-Duha, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever institutes a good practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, there is written for him the like of the reward of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from the reward of whoever acts upon it. And whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, there is written upon him the like of the burden of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"2444","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Karamah narrated: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated: Shayban narrated: from al-Amash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, and from Abu Yazid al-Ansari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal al-Absi, from Jarir, he said: Some Bedouin people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw need and hardship upon them. He addressed the people, praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then commanded them to give charity, urged them to it, and encouraged them in it. They were slow upon him until that was seen in his face. Then a man came with a handful of silver and gave it to him. Then another came, until the people followed one another in charity, until joy was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Whoever institutes a good practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, he will have its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, upon him will be its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"2445","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated (ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated; both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated: from al-Amash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, he said: Some Bedouin people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"2446","Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Narmaqi al-Razi narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated: Mujalid narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal narrated to me, he said: My father sent me to Jarir ibn Abd Allah, he said: Convey greetings to him and say to him: How did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever institutes a righteous practice and is followed in it and it is acted upon? He said: So I went to him and asked him, and he said: He will have the like of the reward of every man who acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice and is followed in it and it is acted upon, upon him will be the like of the sin of every man who acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their sins."
"2447","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated: Shuabah informed us: from al-Amash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"2448","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Hafs narrated: from al-Amash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"2449","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Waki narrated: from al-Amash, from Tamim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"2450","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Jarir narrated: from al-Amash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"2451","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Abu Awanah and Abu Muawiyah narrated: from al-Amash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"2452","Al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated (ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated; both said: Sharik narrated: from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of all good."
"2453","Abu Husayn narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Ali ibn Mushir narrated: from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"2454","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated: from his father, from al-Amash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The freed captives of Quraysh, and the freed slaves of Thaqif, and the Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another."
"2455","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated: Israil informed us: from Shabib ibn Gharqadah, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Mustazill, he said: I heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah, while he was a commander over us, saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I returned, so he called me and said: I will not accept from you until you pledge allegiance to sincere advice to every Muslim. So I pledged allegiance to him."
"2456","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated: Mualla ibn Mansur narrated: Amr ibn Thabit narrated: from his uncle, from Abu Burdah, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gentleness brings increase and blessing, and whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"2457","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah al-Utbi narrated to us: Hibban ibn Nafi ibn Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated: Said ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated: from Mamar ibn al-Hasan, from Bakr ibn Khunays, from Abu Shaybah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a group of his Companions: I shall recite to you verses from the end of al-Zumar; whoever among you weeps, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. He recited it from: And they did not esteem Allah His true esteem, to the end of the surah. Some of us wept and some of us did not weep. Those who did not weep said: O Messenger of Allah, we strove to weep but could not weep. He said: I shall recite it to you; whoever does not weep, let him feign weeping."
"2458","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzad narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated: Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir narrated: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I saw Jarir wipe over the leather socks. The people said: This was only before al-Maidah. Jarir said: I only embraced Islam after al-Maidah, and I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the leather socks."
"2459","Abu Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said al-Kufi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jarir, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Islam, and he stipulated upon me sincere advice to every Muslim. And I am indeed sincere to you all."
"2460","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Jafar ibn Humayd narrated: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated: from Abd al-Malik, from Jarir, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Islam and sincere advice to every Muslim. And I am indeed sincere to you all."
"2461","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah on the pulpit saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he stipulated upon me sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2462","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated (ha), and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated (ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated; they said: Abu Awanah narrated: from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard Jarir saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I pledge allegiance to you upon migration. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my pledge and stipulated upon me sincere advice to every Muslim. So I pledged allegiance to him upon this."
"2463","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated: Israil informed us: from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, that he heard Jarir saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he stipulated upon me sincere advice to every Muslim. By the Lord of the Kabah, I am indeed sincere to you all."
"2464","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated: Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated: from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard Jarir saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine upon Islam, and he stipulated upon me sincere advice to every Muslim. By the Lord of the Kabah, I am indeed sincere to you all."
"2465","Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar narrated: Sufyan narrated: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated, he said: I heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2466","Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Misar, from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim. And I am indeed a sincere adviser to you."
"2467","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us: Ismail b. Zakariya narrated to us: from Asim al-Ahwal, from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, who said: I heard Jarir saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim. And I am an adviser to all of you."
"2468","Al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to give sincere counsel to every Muslim."
"2469","Ahmad b. Dawud al-Makki and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both saying: Amr b. Marzuq narrated to us: Shubah informed us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: I heard him on the day al-Mughirah b. Shubah died, saying: I enjoin upon you fear of Allah, and hear and obey until a commander comes to you. He said: Then he mentioned al-Mughirah and said: Seek forgiveness for him, may Allah pardon you, for he loved well-being. Then he said: As for what follows, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, and he said: And sincere counsel to every Muslim."
"2470","Mahmud b. Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zakariya b. Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us: Waki narrated to us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took our pledge to hear and obey, and to give sincere advice to every Muslim; so I pledged allegiance to him upon Islam and sincere counsel to every Muslim."
"2471","Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Ahmad b. Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, who said: I heard Jarir b. Abdullah saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey, and to give sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2472","Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Adam b. Abi Iyas narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"2473","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Jafar b. Humayd narrated to us: al-Walid b. Abi Thawr narrated to us: from Ziyad, that Jarir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven."
"2474","Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: Harun b. Zayd b. Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us: my father narrated to me: al-Mufaddal b. Sadaqah Abu Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us: from Ziyad, who said: I heard Jarir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven, and whoever does not repent will not be turned to in mercy."
"2475","Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Ali b. Jafar narrated to us: Dawud b. al-Rabi narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi narrated to us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not repent will not be turned to in mercy."
"2476","Abu al-Husayn narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi narrated to us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, from Jarir, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah does not forgive one who does not forgive, and Allah does not show mercy to one who does not show mercy."
"2477","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Bishr b. Adam narrated to us: Yaqub b. Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: Zaidah narrated to us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, from Jarir, who said: A Jewish scholar in Yemen said to me: If your companion is a prophet, then he has died. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died on Monday."
"2478","Ali b. Said al-Razi narrated to us: Isam b. Rawwad b. al-Jarrah narrated to us: Yaqub b. Abi Abbad narrated to us: Sufyan, that is Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us: from Ziyad b. Ilaqah, who said: I heard Jarir b. Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never saw me except that he smiled."
"2479","Al-Mughirah b. Shubayl b. Awf from Jarir: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Habib b. Abi Thabit, from al-Mughirah b. Shubayl, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Any slave who flees, the covenant of protection is absolved from him."
"2480","Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Amr b. Dinar narrated to us: from Habib b. Abi Thabit, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave flees, the protection of Allah is absolved from him. And he did not mention al-Mughirah b. Shubayl."
"2481","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Yunus b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us: from al-Mughirah b. Shubayl, from Jarir, who said: When I drew near Madinah I made my camel kneel, then untied my baggage, put on my robe, and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon. I greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people stared at me. I said to the one sitting beside me: O servant of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention anything about me? He said: Yes, he mentioned you in the best manner; while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering his sermon, something occurred to him in his sermon and he said: There shall enter upon you through this mountain pass, or through this door, one of the best of the people of Yemen; indeed, upon his face is the touch of an angel. He said: So I praised Allah for what He had bestowed upon me."
"2482","Abdullah b. Umayrah from Jarir: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: from Simak b. Harb, from Abdullah b. Umayrah, from Jarir, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, and he withheld his hand until I pledged sincere counsel to every Muslim."
"2483","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Simak, from Abdullah b. Umayrah, from Jarir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2484","Tariq al-Taymi from Jarir: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Amr b. Awn and Muhammad b. Abi Nuaym narrated to us, both saying: Waki narrated to us: from Shubah, from Jabir, from Tariq al-Taymi, from Jarir: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some women and greeted them."
"2485","Amir b. Sad al-Bajali from Jarir: Ali b. Muhammad al-Ansinawi al-Misri narrated to us: Harmalah b. Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Yahya b. Abdullah b. Salim informed me: from Musa b. Uqbah, from Abdullah b. Ali, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir b. Sad al-Bajali, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"2486","Abdullah b. Abdullah al-Subayi from Jarir: Uthman b. Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Raja narrated to us: Israil informed us: from Abu Ishaq, from his father, from Jarir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2487","Ibrahim b. Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us: Amr b. Hakkam narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from his father, from Jarir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2488","Ribi b. Hirash from Jarir: Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yasin, from Hammad b. Abi Sulayman, from Ribi b. Hirash, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he wiped over his leather socks after Surah al-Maidah had been revealed."
"2489","Abu Zibyan al-Janbi Husayn b. Jundub from Jarir: Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ubayd narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"2490","Muadh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Zayd b. Wahb and Abu Zibyan, that they both heard Jarir b. Abdullah narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2491","Abd al-Rahman b. Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl b. Uthman narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah informed us: from al-Amash, from Zayd b. Wahb and Abu Zibyan, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2492","Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Rahawayh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2493","Jafar b. Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Yazid al-Bakri al-Jawzajani narrated to us: Abu Muti al-Balkhi al-Hakam b. Abdullah narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: from Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2494","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah wrote in the Mother of the Book before He created the heavens and the earth: I am the Most Merciful; I created the womb and derived for it a name from My names, so whoever joins it I shall join him, and whoever severs it I shall sever him."
"2495","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Uthman b. Said narrated to us: Abu Waki narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Zibyan, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to those on earth, the One in heaven will not show mercy to him."
"2496","Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. Said al-Qattan narrated to us: Suwayd b. Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us: Abu Kudaynah Yahya b. al-Muhallab narrated to us: from Qabus b. Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was once addressing the people when he said: There has come to you one of the best of the people of Yemen, upon whose face is the touch of an angel, meaning me."
"2497","Abu Ishaq al-Subayi from Jarir: Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jandal b. Waliq narrated to us: Ubaydullah b. Amr narrated to us: from Zayd b. Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Fasting three days of every month is fasting the whole lifetime: the white days, the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth."
"2498","Abdullah b. al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Makhlad b. al-Hasan b. Abi Zumayl narrated to us: Abdullah narrated to us with his chain similarly."
"2499","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yahya b. Adam narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not thank people has not thanked Allah."
"2500","Muadh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from Jarir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Show mercy to those on earth, and the One in heaven will show mercy to you."
"2501","Mujahid from Jarir: Ali b. Said al-Razi narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi al-Nadr narrated to us; (ha) and Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Ziyad b. Abdullah b. Ulathah narrated to me: from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: I only embraced Islam after al-Maidah was revealed, and I only saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over his socks after I had embraced Islam."
"2502","Nafi b. Jubayr b. Mutim from Jarir: Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Amr b. Dinar narrated to us: from Nafi b. Jubayr b. Mutim, from Jarir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2503","Bishr b. Harb from Jarir: Ali b. Said al-Razi narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Salih b. Ruzayq al-Attar narrated to us: Muhammad b. Awn Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us: Harb b. Surayj narrated to us: from Bishr b. Harb, from Jarir, who said: We attended the season of Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was the Farewell Hajj. We reached a place called Ghadir Khumm, and he called out: Prayer in congregation. So the Muhajirun and Ansar gathered, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in our midst and said: O people, to what do you testify? They said: We testify that there is no god but Allah. He said: Then what? They said: And that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He said: So who is your master? They said: Allah and His Messenger are our masters. He said: Who is your master? Then he struck with his hand upon the upper arm of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and raised him, baring his upper arm, and took hold of his forearms and said: Whoever has Allah and His Messenger as his masters, then this one is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. O Allah, whoever among people loves him, be loving to him, and whoever hates him, be hating to him. O Allah, I find no one on earth after the two righteous servants to entrust except you, so decree good concerning him. Bishr said: I said: Who are these two righteous servants? He said: I do not know."
"2504","Muhammad b. Sirin from Jarir b. Abdullah: Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Shayban b. Farrukh narrated to us: Harb b. Surayj al-Minqari narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks."
"2505","Isa b. Jariyah al-Ansari from Jarir: Amr b. Abi al-Tahir b. al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us: Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: from Said b. Muhammad al-Ansari, from Isa b. Jariyah al-Ansari, from Jarir al-Bajali, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the leather socks. It was said to him: After Surah al-Maidah was revealed? He said: And did I embrace Islam except after Surah al-Maidah was revealed."
"2506","Abu Bakr b. Amr b. Utbah from Jarir: Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Muawiyah b. Amr narrated to us: al-Masudi narrated to us: from Abu Bakr, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Islam, and he withheld his hand so as to stipulate upon me sincere counsel to every Muslim."
"2507","Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Harith al-Taymi from Jarir: Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Yahya b. Muhammad b. al-Sakan narrated to us: Ishaq b. Idris narrated to us: Bakkar, the nephew of Musa b. Ubaydah, narrated to us: from Musa b. Ubaydah, from Muhammad b. Ibrahim, from Jarir: That some people of Uraynah raided the milk camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that their hands and feet be cut off and their eyes be branded."
"2508","Awn b. Abdullah b. Utbah b. Masud from Jarir: Abdan b. Ahmad and Ibrahim b. Mattawayh al-Asbahani narrated to us, both saying: al-Hasan b. Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us: Bakr b. Sadaqah narrated to us; (ha) and Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Shuayb al-Dujani narrated to us: Yahya b. Hakim narrated to us: Hammad b. Masadah narrated to us, both from Ibn Ajlan, from Awn b. Abdullah b. Utbah, from Jarir al-Bajali: That when he would put up goods for sale he would point out their defects and then give the buyer the choice, saying: If you wish, take it, and if you wish, leave it. It was said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, if you do this no sale will go through for you. He said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to give sincere counsel to the people of Islam."
"2509","Shahr b. Hawshab from Jarir b. Abdullah: Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Haywah b. Shurayh al-Himsi narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn b. al-Sumayda al-Antaki narrated to us: Musa b. Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us: Baqiyyah b. al-Walid narrated to us; (ha) and Musa b. Harun narrated to us: Hajib b. al-Walid narrated to us: Abu Haywah Shurayh b. Yazid al-Himsi narrated to us, the latter two saying: Ibrahim b. Adham narrated to us: from Muqatil b. Hayyan, from Shahr b. Hawshab, from Jarir, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."
"2510","Damrah b. Habib from Jarir: Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abdah b. Abdullah al-Saffar narrated to us: Zayd b. al-Hubab narrated to us: Muawiyah b. Salih narrated to us: from Damrah b. Habib, from Jarir, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the revelation of al-Maidah, and I saw him wiping over the leather socks."
"2511","Jandarh b. Khayshanah Abu Qirsafah al-Laythi, freedman of Banu Layth b. Bakr b. Abd Manah b. Kinanah: Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah al-Asqalani narrated to us: Ayyub b. Ali b. al-Haytham narrated to us: Ziyad b. Sayyar narrated to us: Azzah bint Iyad b. Abi Qirsafah narrated to me, saying: I heard my grandfather Abu Qirsafah, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The beginning of my Islam was that I was an orphan between my mother and my maternal aunt, and my affection inclined mostly to my aunt. I used to graze some small sheep of mine, and my aunt would often say to me: O my son, do not go to this man, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), lest he mislead you and lead you astray. I would go out until I came to the pasture, leave my small sheep, then come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and remain with him listening to him, then return in the evening with my sheep lean with dry udders. My aunt said to me: Why are your sheep dry-uddered? I said: I do not know. Then I returned to him on the second day and did as on the first day, except that I heard him saying: O people, emigrate and hold fast to Islam, for emigration does not cease as long as jihad remains. Then I returned with my sheep as on the first day. Then I returned to him on the third day and remained with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) listening to him until I embraced Islam, pledged allegiance to him, and shook his hand with my hand. I complained to him about my aunt and my sheep, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Bring me the sheep. So I brought them to him; he wiped their backs and udders and supplicated for blessing in them, and they filled out with fat and milk. When I entered upon my aunt with them she said: O my son, graze like this. I said: O aunt, I grazed only where I grazed every day, but let me tell you my story. So I told her the story, my coming to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and told her of his conduct and speech. My mother and aunt said to me: Take us to him. So I went, I and my mother and aunt, and they embraced Islam and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but they did not shake hands. This is what happened of the Islam of Abu Qirsafah and his emigration to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ziyad said: And Abu Qirsafah used to dwell in the land of Tihamah."
"2512","Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah al-Asqalani narrated to us: Ayyub b. Ali b. al-Haytham narrated to us: Ziyad b. Sayyar narrated to us: from Azzah bint Iyad, who said: I heard Abu Qirsafah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do you have offspring? I said: I have a brother. He said: Then bring him. So I treated my brother gently, and he was a small boy, until he came with me. When he drew near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he fled, so I seized him and held his hands and feet together, then brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his pledge. His name was Maysam, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What is his name, O Abu Qirsafah? I said: His name is Maysam. He said: Rather his name is Muslim. I said: Muslim, with you, O Messenger of Allah."
"2513","Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah narrated to us: Ayyub b. Ali b. al-Haytham narrated to us: Ziyad b. Sayyar narrated to us: from Azzah, from Abu Qirsafah, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclining on his back, placing one of his legs upon the other."
"2514","Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah narrated to us: Ayyub b. Ali b. al-Haytham narrated to us: Ziyad b. Sayyar narrated to us: from Azzah, who said: I heard Abu Qirsafah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Narrate from me what you hear, and it is not lawful for a man to lie about me; whoever lies about me, and says about me what I did not say, a house in Hell is built for him in which he shall graze."
"2515","Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah narrated to us: Ayyub b. Ali b. al-Haytham narrated to us: Ziyad b. Sayyar narrated to us: from Azzah bint Iyad, who said: I heard Abu Qirsafah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar, may Allah forgive them; and Aslam, may Allah grant them safety."
"2516","Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah narrated to us: Ayyub b. Ali b. al-Haytham narrated to us: Ziyad b. Sayyar narrated to us: from Azzah bint Iyad, who said: I heard Abu Qirsafah saying: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and my mother and my aunt, and we returned from him departing, my mother and aunt said to me: O my son, we have never seen a man like this, more handsome of face, cleaner of garment, nor softer of speech; and we saw as though light was issuing from his mouth."
"2517","Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us: from Ziyad, from Azzah bint Iyad, who said: I heard Abu Qirsafah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves a people, Allah will gather him among their company."
"2518","Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us: Ziyad narrated to us: from Azzah bint Iyad, who said: I heard Abu Qirsafah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me with a hooded cloak and said: Wear it."
"2519","Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah narrated to us: Ayyub b. Ali narrated to us: Ziyad b. Sayyar narrated to us: from Azzah bint Iyad, who said: I heard Abu Qirsafah that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Build mosques and remove filth from them; whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and these mosques built along the road? He said: Yes; and removing filth from them is the dowry of the houris."
"2520","Yahya b. Uthman b. Salih narrated to us: Yunus b. Abd al-Rahim al-Asqalani narrated to me: Ayyash b. Marthad al-Kinani narrated to me: my uncle Atiyah b. Said narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Qirsafah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, do not disgrace me on the day of battle, and do not disgrace me on the Day of Resurrection."
"2521","Muhammad b. al-Khazr al-Tabarani narrated to us: Ayyub b. Ali b. al-Haytham narrated to us: Ziyad b. Sayyar narrated to us: Azzah bint Iyad b. Abi Qirsafah narrated to me, saying: The Romans captured a son of Abu Qirsafah, and whenever the time of a prayer came, Abu Qirsafah would ascend the walls of Asqalan and call out: O so-and-so, prayer; and he would hear him while in the land of the Romans."
"2522","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Hamid narrated to us: Abdullah b. al-Mubarak narrated to us: Yahya b. Hassan narrated to us: a shaykh of Banu Kinanah narrated to me, saying: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard him saying: O Allah, do not disgrace me on the Day of Resurrection, and do not disgrace me on the day of battle."
"2523","Chapter of Ha: al-Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, known as Abu Muhammad; mention of the birth of al-Hasan b. Ali, his description and death, may Allah be pleased with him. Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr saying: al-Hasan b. Ali was known as Abu Muhammad."
"2524","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Uthman b. Said al-Murri narrated to us: Ali b. Salih narrated to us: from Simak b. Harb, from Qabus b. al-Mukhariq al-Shaybani, from his father, who said: Umm al-Fadl came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw a part of your body within me. He said: What a good thing you saw; Fatimah shall give birth to a boy, and you shall nurse him with the milk of Qutham. He said: Then she brought him, carrying him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and placed him in his lap, and he urinated; so she struck him with her hand. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have hurt my son, may Allah have mercy on you. She said: Give me your waist-wrapper so we may wash it. He said: Only the urine of a girl is washed; the urine of a boy is sprinkled over."
"2525","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. al-Hakam b. Abi Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us: from Sufyan, from Umar b. Said, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Uqbah b. al-Harith, who said: I was with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, when he passed by al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and placed him upon his neck and said: By my father, he resembles the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not Ali. He said: And Ali was with him, and he began to laugh, may Allah be pleased with them all."
"2526","Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Uthman b. Said b. Abi Husayn narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Uqbah b. al-Harith, who said: I went out with Abu Bakr. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"2527","Zakariya b. Hamdawayh al-Saffar al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Affan b. Muslim narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad narrated to us: from Asim b. Kulayb, from his father, who said: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, was mentioned in the presence of Ibn Abbas, and he said: He used to resemble the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2528","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Warith b. Abd al-Samad b. Abd al-Warith narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhtasib Abu Aidh narrated to us: Shuja b. Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that he saw al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, with his hair striking his shoulders."
"2529","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ubadah b. Ziyad narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Abi Zuhayr, the freedman of al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, dyeing with woad. Al-Hadrami said: Thus Ubadah said: the freedman of al-Hasan, but he is in fact the freedman of al-Husayn."
"2530","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Abi Zuhayr al-Nakhai, who said: I saw al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, dyeing with black."
"2531","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Hudbah b. Khalid narrated to us: al-Ala b. Khalid al-Riyahi narrated to us: from Zadham Abu Mansur, who said: I saw al-Hasan b. Ali dyeing with henna and katam."
"2532","Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. Amir b. Ibrahim al-Asbahani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: from my grandfather Amir: from Yaqub al-Qummi: from Anbasah b. Said, from Ibrahim b. Muhajir, from al-Shabi: that al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to dye with black."
"2533","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Muawiyah b. Hisham narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Ismail b. Raja, from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father: that al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to dye with black."
"2534","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Warith b. Abd al-Samad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhtasib Abu Aidh narrated to us: Shuja b. Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that he saw al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, dyed black upon a long-legged horse."
"2535","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Jumhur b. Mansur narrated to us: Muhammad b. Rabiah narrated to us: from Mustaqim b. Abd al-Malik, who said: I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, young, and they did not dye."
"2536","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibn al-Salt narrated to us: from Abu Shihab, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from al-Hasan b. Zayd, from his father, who said: I saw a tuft on the head of al-Hasan; I saw al-Hasan pulling it until he drew it near."
"2537","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Tahir b. Abi Ahmad narrated to us: Man b. Isa narrated to us: from Sulayman b. Bilal, from Jafar, from his father, that he said: al-Hasan used to wear his ring on his left hand."
"2538","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ubaydullah al-Muharibi narrated to us: Hatim b. Ismail narrated to us: from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father, who said: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to wear his ring on his left hand."
"2539","Al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Simak b. Harb, from Qabus b. al-Mukhariq, from Umm al-Fadl, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw in a dream as though a limb of your limbs was in my house, or she said: in my chamber. He said: Fatimah shall give birth to a boy, Allah willing, and you shall take charge of him. She said: Then Fatimah gave birth to Hasan, and he was handed to her and she nursed him with the milk of Qutham b. al-Abbas. She said: One day I brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he urinated upon his chest, so I struck his back. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, may Allah have mercy on you; you have hurt my son. I said: Hand me your waist-wrapper and I shall wash it. He said: No; pour water upon it, for water is poured upon the urine of a boy, while the urine of a girl is washed."
"2540","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Nuaym Dirar b. Surad narrated to us: Muhammad b. Fudayl narrated to us: from Ali b. Muyassir, from Umar b. Umayr, from Urwah b. Fayruz, from Surah bint Mishrah, who said: I was among those who attended Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, when labor seized her, among some women. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: How is she? I said: She is in great distress, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When she delivers, do not precede me in anything concerning him. She said: Then she delivered, and they tied his cord and wrapped him in a yellow rag. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: What did she do? I said: She has given birth to a boy, and I tied his cord and wrapped him in a rag. He said: You have disobeyed me. She said: I seek refuge with Allah from disobeying Allah and from the anger of His Messenger. He said: Bring him to me. So I brought him to him; he cast aside the yellow rag, wrapped him in a white rag, spat in his mouth, and fed him with his saliva. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came, and he said: What have you named him, O Ali? He said: I named him Jafar, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No, but Hasan; and after him Husayn; and you are Abu Hasan al-Khayr."
"2541","Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The one among them who most resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2542","Muadh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us: from Ismail b. Abi Khalid, from Abu Juhayfah, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him."
"2543","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Masud Ahmad b. al-Furat narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Qays narrated to us: from Harun b. al-Mughirah, from Amr b. Abi Qays, from Yazid b. Abi Maryam, from al-Bahiyy, who said: We were discussing the resemblance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If you wish to look at one who resembled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then look at al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2544","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us: Muhammad b. Bishr narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us, saying: Abu Juhayfah said to me: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him."
"2545","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ishaq b. Shahin narrated to us: Khalid b. Abdullah narrated to us: from Ismail, from Abu Juhayfah, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him."
"2546","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us: Yazid b. Harun narrated to us: from Ismail b. Abi Khalid, who said: I said to Abu Juhayfah: Did you see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; and the one among people who most resembled him was al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2547","Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abdullah b. Idris narrated to us: from Ismail, from Abu Juhayfah, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him."
"2548","Muhammad b. Ali Fustuqah narrated to us: Dawud b. Rushayd narrated to us: from al-Haytham b. Adi, who said: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, died in the year forty-four. Thus al-Haytham b. Adi said, and he was contradicted."
"2549","Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, died in the year forty-eight."
"2550","Ubayd narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yahya b. Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: from Abu Bakr b. Hafs, who said: Sad and al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, died in the year forty-eight."
"2551","Ubayd narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yahya b. Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: from Abu Bakr b. Hafs, who said: Sad and al-Hasan b. Ali died after ten years of the rule of Muawiyah had passed, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2552","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr saying: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, died at the age of forty-seven."
"2553","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr saying: al-Hasan b. Ali died in the year forty-eight."
"2554","Abu al-Zinba narrated to us: Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan b. Ali died in the year forty-nine, and Said b. al-As prayed over him; his death was in Madinah, his age forty-six or forty-seven, and he was known as Abu Muhammad."
"2555","Al-Miqdam b. Dawud narrated to us: Ali b. Mabad narrated to us: Ubaydullah b. Amr narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Aqil, who said: The tribulation lasted five years; of that, four months belonged to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him; and the unity was upon Muawiyah in the year forty."
"2556","Muhammad b. Ali al-Madini narrated to us: Abu Zayd Umar b. Shabbah narrated to us: from Abu Nuaym, who said: And in it died al-Hasan b. Ali and Sad b. Abi Waqqas in the year fifty-eight."
"2557","Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ali b. al-Madini narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, who said: I witnessed al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, at al-Nukhaylah when Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, made peace with him. Muawiyah said to him: When this happens, stand and speak, and inform the people that you have handed this affair over to me. And perhaps Sufyan said: Inform the people of this affair which you have left for me. So he stood and addressed from the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him; al-Shabi said: and I was listening. Then he said: As for what follows, the shrewdest shrewdness is piety, and the most foolish folly is immorality; and this affair over which I and Muawiyah differed, either it was a right of mine which I left to Muawiyah seeking the welfare of this ummah and sparing their blood, or it was a right belonging to one more entitled to it than me, and I did that; and I do not know, perhaps it is a trial for you and enjoyment for a time."
"2558","Muhammad b. Jafar b. Ayan al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Dawud b. Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us: Asbat b. Muhammad narrated to us: from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr b. al-Asamm, who said: I entered upon al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, while he was in the house of Amr b. Hurayth, and said: Some people claim that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, will return before the Day of Resurrection. He laughed and said: Glory be to Allah; had we known that, we would not have married off his wives nor divided his inheritance."
"2559","Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abdullah, from his father, from al-Hasan b. Sad, from his father, who said: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, gave two women as parting-gift twenty thousand and a skin of honey. One of them, and I think she was Hanafiyyah, said: A small provision from a beloved who is parting."
"2560","Remaining reports of al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil b. Yunus, from Abu Ishaq, who said: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, gave a woman as parting-gift twenty thousand; when it was brought to her and placed before her, she said: A small provision from a beloved who is parting."
"2561","Sahl b. Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Quraysh b. Anas narrated to us: Ibn Awn narrated to us: from Muhammad, who said: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, proposed to the daughter of Manzur b. Sayyar b. Rayyan al-Fazari. He said: By Allah, I shall marry you to her, though I know you to be quick to marry, quick to divorce, and ingratiating; except that you are the noblest of Arabs in house and noblest in lineage."
"2562","Al-Husayn b. Ishaq narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Ala narrated to us: from Hisham b. Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, who said: al-Hasan b. Ali married a woman, and sent to her one hundred slave-girls, with each slave-girl a thousand dirhams."
"2563","Ibrahim b. Nailah and Muhammad b. Nusayr al-Asbahaniyan narrated to us, both saying: Ismail b. Amr al-Bajali narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both saying: Ubayd b. Wasim narrated to us: Abu Shaddad narrated to us, saying: I used to play at knucklebones with al-Hasan and al-Husayn; when they beat me they rode upon me, and when I beat them they said: Would you ride a part of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"2564","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: al-Hasan b. al-Rabi narrated to us: from Salim Abu Abdullah, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, who said: I asked Ata: May I carry Zamzam water? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried it, and al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, carried it."
"2565","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"2566","Musa b. Harun narrated to us: Ahmad b. Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim b. Tahman narrated to us: from al-Hajjaj b. al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn."
"2567","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us: Abdullah b. al-Ajlah narrated to us: from Yahya b. Said, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The aqiqah was performed for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"2568","Ali b. Said al-Kindi narrated to us: al-Muharibi narrated to us: from Yahya b. Said, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the aqiqah was performed for Hasan and Husayn."
"2569","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abbad b. Ahmad al-Arzami narrated to us: my uncle narrated to us: from his father: from Amr b. Qays, from Atiyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: As for Hasan, Husayn and Muhassin, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named them, performed the aqiqah for them, shaved their heads, gave charity of their weight, commanded concerning them, and their navel-cords were cut and they were circumcised."
"2570","Muadh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Muhammad b. Jabir narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from one of his companions, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"2571","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Sahl b. Zanjalah al-Razi and al-Hasan b. Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, both saying: Shabbabah b. Sawwar narrated to us: from al-Mughirah b. Muslim, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"2572","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Mahmud b. Ghaylan narrated to us: Ali b. al-Hasan b. Shaqiq narrated to us: al-Husayn b. Waqid narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"2573","Ahmad b. Yahya b. Khalid b. Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us: Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: from Umarah b. Ghaziyyah, from Rabiah b. Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas b. Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded concerning the heads of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, the sons of Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with them, on the seventh day, and it was shaved; then he gave charity of its weight in silver, and found no sacrificial animal."
"2574","Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Musa b. Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us; (ha) and Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Mualla b. Mahdi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Aqil, from Ali b. al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi, who said: When Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, gave birth to Hasan, she said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not perform the aqiqah for my son? He said: No; but shave his head and give charity of the weight of his hair in wariq, or he said: silver, upon the poor. When she gave birth to Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, she did the like with him. And Musa b. Dawud said in his narration: upon the destitute and the poor. And Abu al-Qasim said: al-awfad are the poor."
"2575","Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: Said b. Abi al-Rabi al-Samman narrated to us: Said b. Salamah b. Abi al-Husam narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Aqil, from Ali b. al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi: that when Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, gave birth to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, she wanted to perform the aqiqah for him with a great ram. She came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do not perform the aqiqah for him with anything; but shave the hair of his head, then give charity of its weight in silver in the path of Allah, or upon the destitute. Then she gave birth to al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, the following year, and did the like with him."
"2576","Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri; (ha) and Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Asim b. Ubaydullah, from Ubaydullah b. Abi Rafi, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) call the adhan of prayer in the ear of al-Hasan b. Ali when Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with them both, gave birth to him."
"2577","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Awn b. Sallam and Jubarah b. Mughallis narrated to us, both saying: Hammad b. Shuayb narrated to us: from Asim b. Ubaydullah, from Ali b. al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the adhan in the ears of al-Hasan and al-Husayn when they were born, and commanded it."
"2578","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: from Ibn Awn, from Umayr b. Ishaq: that Abu Hurayrah met al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, and said: Lift your garment so I may kiss where I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss. So he lifted from his belly, and he placed his hand upon his navel."
"2579","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Abd al-Salam b. Harb narrated to us: from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Yazid b. Yuhannis, from Said b. Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced Hasan, then said: O Allah, I have loved him, so love him."
"2580","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Adi b. Thabit informed us, saying: I heard al-Bara b. Azib saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with al-Hasan b. Ali upon his shoulder, saying: O Allah, I love him, so love him."
"2581","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Fudayl b. Marzuq narrated to us: from Adi b. Thabit, from al-Bara b. Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: O Allah, I have loved him, so love him and love whoever loves him."
"2582","Ahmad b. Amr al-Qitrani narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Tufayl narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Ashath b. Sawwar, from Adi b. Thabit, from al-Bara b. Azib, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carrying al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, upon his shoulder, saying: O Allah, I love Hasan, so love him."
"2583","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Abi al-Wazir narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi al-Kannat narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take Hasan and draw him to himself, saying: O Allah, this is my son, so love him, and love whoever loves him."
"2584","Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah b. Salih narrated to us: Muawiyah b. Salih narrated to me: from Rashid b. Sad, from Yala b. Murrah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when we were invited to food, and Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was playing in the road. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened ahead of the people, then spread out his hands; Husayn kept running one time here and one time there, and he kept making him laugh until he took him. He placed one of his hands upon his chin and the other between his head and his ears, then embraced him and kissed him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Husayn is from me and I am from him; may Allah love whoever loves him; al-Hasan and al-Husayn are two grandsons among the grandsons."
"2585","Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: al-Abbas b. al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: Yahya b. Sulaym narrated to us: Abdullah b. Uthman b. Khuthaym narrated to us: from Said b. Abi Rashid, from Yala b. Murrah: that Hasan and Husayn came walking toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when one of them came he placed his hand upon his neck, then the other came and he placed his other hand upon his neck, kissed this one, then kissed this one, then said: O Allah, I love them both, so love them both. O people, children are a cause of miserliness and cowardice."
"2586","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim b. Ibrahim and Arim narrated to us, both saying: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us: from Ali b. Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon, al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, climbed up to him; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced him and said: This son of mine is a leader, and perhaps Allah, Mighty and Majestic, shall reconcile through him between two groups of Muslims."
"2587","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Muhammad al-Qawwash narrated to us: Muslim b. Khalid narrated to us: from Ibn Khaytham, from Said b. Abi Rashid, from Yala b. Murrah al-Amiri: that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to food to which they had been invited, and Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was playing with children. He came toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who spread out his hand; the boy kept fleeing here and there, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept making him laugh until he took him. He placed one of his hands upon his neck and the other upon the crown of his head, then embraced him and kissed him, then said: Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn; may Allah love whoever loves Husayn; Husayn is a grandson among the grandsons."
"2588","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me; (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us: from Israil Abu Musa, from al-Hasan, who said: Abu Bakrah narrated to me, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the pulpit, with al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, beside him; he would look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a glance, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would look at him a glance, saying: This son of mine is a leader, and perhaps Allah shall reconcile through him between two groups of Muslims."
"2589","Muhammad b. Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Mubarak b. Fadalah narrated to us: from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be praying, and al-Hasan would come, being a small young boy; whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he would leap upon his neck and back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his head with a gentle raising until he set him down. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you do with this boy something we have not seen you do. He said: He is my sweet basil of this world; this son of mine is a leader, and perhaps Allah shall reconcile through him between two groups of Muslims."
"2590","Jafar b. Muhammad al-Naysaburi narrated to us: al-Rabi b. Sulayman narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Shaybah al-Juddi narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: from Yunus and Mansur, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, with him, saying: This son of mine is a leader, and Allah shall reconcile at his hands between two great groups of Muslims."
"2591","Ahmad b. Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us: Ashath b. Abd al-Malik narrated to us: from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: This son of mine is a leader, and I hope Allah shall reconcile through him between two groups of my ummah."
"2592","Abd al-Rahman b. Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl b. Uthman narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: from Ismail b. Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day, with Hasan and Husayn with him; when he prostrated, al-Hasan came and leapt upon his back. Whenever he raised his head he would steady him lest he fall. When he finished, he took his hand and seated him in his lap and kissed him, and said: This son of mine is a leader, and he is my sweet basil in this world; and I hope Allah shall reconcile through him between two great groups of Muslims."
"2593","Ahmad b. Abdullah al-Bazzar al-Tustari narrated to us: Ubaydullah b. Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us: from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: This son of mine is a leader, and I surely hope Allah shall reconcile through him between two groups of my ummah."
"2594","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. al-Hakam b. Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us: Zayd b. al-Hubab narrated to us: Muhammad b. Salih al-Tammar al-Madani narrated to us: Muslim b. Abi Maryam narrated to me: from al-Maqburi, who said: We were with Abu Hurayrah when al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, came and greeted him; the people returned his greeting, and he passed while Abu Hurayrah did not know. It was said to him: This is Hasan b. Ali greeting. So he caught up with him and said: And upon you, O my master. It was said to him: You say, O my master? He said: I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is a leader."
"2595","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Salam b. Asim al-Razi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Maghra narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This son of mine, meaning al-Hasan, is a leader, and Allah shall surely reconcile through him between two groups of Muslims."
"2596","Muhammad b. Awn al-Sirafi narrated to us: Abu al-Ashath Ahmad b. al-Miqdam narrated to us: Abu Sumayr Hakim b. Khidham narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Shurayh the judge, from Umar b. al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2597","Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2598","Abu al-Zinba Rawh b. al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us: Yazid b. Mawhab al-Ramli narrated to us: Masruh Abu Shihab narrated to us: from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2599","Al-Qasim b. Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us: Mukhawwal b. Ibrahim narrated to us: Mansur b. Abi al-Aswad narrated to us: from Layth, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2600","Al-Qasim b. Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us: Muhammad b. Aban narrated to us: from Abu Janab, from al-Shabi, from Zayd b. Yuthay, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2601","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Uthman b. Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us: Ali b. Thabit narrated to us: Asbat b. Nasr narrated to us: from Jabir, from Abdullah b. Yahya, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her: By Allah, there is no prophet except that the children of prophets are other than me; your two sons are the leaders of the youth of Paradise, except the two sons of the maternal aunt, Yahya and Isa."
"2602","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Muhammad b. Marwan al-Dhuhli narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to me: Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An angel from heaven who had never visited me sought permission from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to visit me, and gave me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2603","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Jumhur b. Mansur narrated to us: Yusuf b. Muhammad narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Abu al-Jahhaf and Habib b. Abi Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2604","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Asim b. Ali narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi narrated to us: Maysarah b. Habib narrated to me: from Adi b. Thabit, from Zirr b. Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is an angel among the angels who sought permission from his Lord to greet me and visit me; he had never descended to earth before it, and he gave me glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2605","Abd al-Aziz b. Yaqub Abu al-Asbagh al-Qaysarani narrated to us: Muhammad b. Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: from Maysarah b. Habib, from al-Minhal b. Amr, from Zirr b. Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2606","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: al-Haytham b. Kharijah narrated to us: Abu al-Aswad Abdullah b. Amir al-Hashimi narrated to us: from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We saw joy upon the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have seen upon your face the heralds of joy. He said: And how should I not rejoice, when Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and gave me glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise, and their father is better than them."
"2607","Muhammad b. al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us: Ubayd b. Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us: Ata b. Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us: Abu Amrah al-Ashjai narrated to me: from Salim b. Abi al-Jad, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I spent the night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw a figure with him. He said to me: O Hudhayfah, did you see? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This is an angel who has not descended to me since I was sent; he came to me tonight and gave me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2608","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: al-Hakam b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Nuaym al-Bajali narrated to us: my father narrated to me: from Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise, except the two sons of the maternal aunt, Isa son of Maryam and Yahya b. Zakariya."
"2609","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Yazid b. Mardanubah narrated to us: from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Nuaym, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2610","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I found in the book of Uqbah b. Qabisah: my father narrated to us: from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Nuaym, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"2611","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Muawiyah b. Hisham narrated to us: Ali b. Qadim narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Abi Nu'm, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasan and Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise."
"2612","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Harb b. al-Hasan al-Tahhan narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Safwan b. Sulaym, from Ata b. Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise."
"2613","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Suwayd b. Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise."
"2614","Ahmad b. Amr al-Qitrani also narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Tufayl narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman b. Sabit, from Jabir b. Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasan and Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise."
"2615","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Minjab b. al-Harith narrated to us: Ali b. Mushir narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman b. Ziyad b. An'um, from Muawiyah b. Qurrah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise, and their father is better than them."
"2616","Muhammad b. al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us: Ismail Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Jassas, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah b. Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise; O Allah, I love them, so love them."
"2617","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, both saying: Abu Ghassan Malik b. Ismail narrated to us: Asbat b. Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Subayh, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Zayd b. Arqam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali, Fatimah, Hasan and al-Husayn: I am at peace with those who are at peace with you, and at war with those who are at war with you."
"2618","Muhammad b. Rashid narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us: Husayn b. Muhammad narrated to us: Sulayman b. Qarm narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Ibrahim b. Abd al-Rahman b. Subayh, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, from his grandfather, from Zayd b. Arqam, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a house in which were Fatimah, Ali, Hasan and Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them, and said: I am at war with those who are at war with you, and at peace with those who are at peace with you."
"2619","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Talid b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Ali, al-Hasan, al-Husayn and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with them, and said: I am at war with those who are at war with you, and at peace with those who are at peace with you."
"2620","Abd al-Rahman b. Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Imran narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Amr b. Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Fakhitah, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited us and spent the night with us while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were asleep. al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to a waterskin of ours and began squeezing it into a cup, then came to give him drink and handed it to al-Hasan. al-Husayn reached out to drink, but he stopped him and began with al-Hasan. Fatimah said: O Messenger of Allah, as if he is the more beloved of the two to you. He said: He asked for water first. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and these two - and I think he said: and this sleeping one - meaning Ali - will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection."
"2621","Abd al-Rahman b. Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Yahya b. Durays al-Faydi narrated to us: Isa b. Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Umar b. Ali narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I, Fatimah, Hasan and Husayn will be gathered together, along with those who love us, on the Day of Resurrection; we shall eat and drink until the servants are separated. That reached a man among the people, so he asked about it and I informed him, and he said: What about the presentation and the reckoning? So I said to him: How was it for the companion of Ya Sin in that, when he was admitted to Paradise at once?"
"2622","Ahmad b. Muhammad al-Murri al-Qantari narrated to us: Harb b. al-Hasan al-Tahhan narrated to us: Yahya b. Ya'la narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ubaydullah b. Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: The first four to enter Paradise are I, you, al-Hasan and al-Husayn; our descendants will be behind our backs, our wives behind our descendants, and our partisans on our right and on our left."
"2623","al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari, Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal and Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Muawiyah b. Hisham narrated to us, from Amr b. Ghiyath, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fatimah guarded her chastity, and Allah, mighty and majestic, will admit her and her offspring to Paradise because of her guarding her chastity."
"2624","Abdullah b. Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Ahmad b. Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim b. Tahman narrated to us, from Abbad b. Ishaq, from Zayd b. Abi al-Attab, from Ubayd b. Jurayj, from Abdullah b. Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the pulpit addressing the people, when al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came out with a cloth around his neck which he was dragging; he stumbled in it and fell on his face. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down from the pulpit heading for him, and when the people saw him they took the boy and brought him to him, so he carried him and said: May Allah destroy Satan; children are a trial. By Allah, I did not realize that I had come down from the pulpit until he was brought to me."
"2625","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ibrahim b. Salih al-Asadi narrated to us: Nafi' b. Hurmuz narrated to us, from Anas b. Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was lying in one of his houses on his back, al-Hasan came crawling until he sat on the chest of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then urinated on his chest. I came to remove him from him, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up and said: Woe to you, O Anas, leave my son and the fruit of my heart; whoever harms him has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water and poured it over the urine, pouring, and said: The urine of a boy is poured over, and the urine of a girl is washed."
"2626","Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Haywah b. Shurayh narrated to us: Baqiyyah b. al-Walid narrated to us, from Bahir b. Sa'd, from Khalid b. Ma'dan, who said: al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib and Amr b. al-Aswad came as a delegation to Qinnasrin, and Muawiyah, may Allah have mercy on him, said to al-Miqdam: Did you know that al-Hasan b. Ali has died? So al-Miqdam said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. Muawiyah said to him: Do you consider it a calamity? He said: Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed him in his lap and said: This one is from me, and Husayn is from Ali."
"2627","Yahya b. Uthman b. Salih narrated to us: Abdullah b. Salih narrated to us: Yahya b. Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad b. Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection upon mounts to attend the gathering place of their day; Salih will be raised upon his she-camel, I shall be raised upon al-Buraq, and my two sons al-Hasan and al-Husayn will be raised upon two she-camels from the she-camels of Paradise."
"2628","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ubadah b. Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us: Yahya b. al-Ala al-Razi narrated to us, from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, placed the offspring of every prophet in his backbone, and Allah, most high, placed my offspring in the backbone of Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2629","Muhammad b. Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us: Bishr b. Mihran narrated to us: Sharik b. Abdullah narrated to us, from Shabib b. Gharqadah, from al-Mustazill b. Husayn, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every child of a female - their paternal kinship is to their father - except the children of Fatimah, for I am their paternal kin and I am their father."
"2630","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Shaybah b. Na'amah, from Fatimah bint Husayn, from Fatimah al-Kubra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child of a mother is ascribed to a paternal kin, except the children of Fatimah; I am their guardian and I am their paternal kin."
"2631","Jafar b. Muhammad b. Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madini narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, who said: Umar b. al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, called Ali b. Abi Talib and spoke to him privately. Then Ali stood and came to al-Suffah, where he found al-Abbas, Aqil and al-Husayn, and consulted them about marrying Umm Kulthum to Umar. Aqil became angry and said: O Ali, the days, months and years only increase you in blindness in your affair; by Allah, if you do it, such-and-such will happen - listing things. And he went off dragging his garment. Ali said to al-Abbas: By Allah, that from him is not sincere advice, but the stick of Umar drove him to what you see. By Allah, that is not out of desire for you, O Aqil, but Umar b. al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every tie and lineage will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, laughed and said: Woe to Aqil, a foolish simpleton."
"2632","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Ubadah b. Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us: Yunus b. Abi Ya'fur narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah b. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every tie and lineage on the Day of Resurrection will be cut off except my tie and my lineage."
"2633","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Sahl al-Hannat narrated to us: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, who said: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every tie and lineage will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage."
"2634","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim b. Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Abi Jafar narrated to us: Ali b. Zayd b. Jud'an narrated to us, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of my Household is like the parable of the ark of Nuh: whoever boards it is saved, whoever stays back from it drowns; and whoever fights us at the end of time, it is as if he fought alongside al-Dajjal."
"2635","al-Husayn b. Ahmad b. Mansur Sajjadah narrated to us: Abdullah b. Dahir al-Razi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Hanash b. al-Mu'tamir, who said: I saw Abu Dharr holding the two doorposts of the Ka'bah, saying: Whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am Abu Dharr al-Ghifari; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The parable of my Household among you is like the parable of the ark of Nuh among the people of Nuh: whoever boards it is saved, whoever stays back from it perishes; and like the gate of Hittah among the Children of Israel."
"2636","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim b. Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Abu al-Sahba, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of my Household is like the parable of the ark of Nuh: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays back from it drowns."
"2637","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Yahya b. Ma'in narrated to us: Hisham b. Yusuf narrated to us, from Abdullah b. Sulayman al-Nawfali, from Muhammad b. Ali b. Abdullah b. Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love Allah for the sustenance He provides you from His blessings, love me for the love of Allah, and love my Household for my love."
"2638","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Jandal b. Waliq narrated to us: Muhammad b. Habib al-Ijli narrated to us, from Ibrahim b. al-Hasan, from Ziyad b. al-Mundhir, from Abd al-Rahman b. Mas'ud al-Abdi, from Ulaym, from Salman, who said: Give the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the rank of the head from the body, and the rank of the eye from the head; for the body is not guided except by the head, and the head is not guided except by the two eyes."
"2639","Muhammad b. Abdullah narrated to us: Harb b. al-Hasan al-Tahhan narrated to us: Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, from Qays b. al-Rabi', from al-A'mash, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When (Say, I do not ask you for any reward except love for kinship) was revealed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these relatives of yours whose love has become obligatory upon us? He said: Ali, Fatimah and their two sons."
"2640","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hawdhah b. Khalifah narrated to us: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah b. Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take me and al-Husayn, seating one of us on his right thigh and the other on his left thigh, and say: O Allah, I love them, so love them."
"2641","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Hafs b. Rashid al-Hilali narrated to us: al-Husayn b. Ali narrated to us: Warqa b. Umar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Husayn b. Ali: Whoever loves him has loved me."
"2642","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Salih al-Azdi narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were on his back, so the people moved them away, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them; may my father and mother be sacrificed for them - whoever loves me, let him love these two."
"2643","Fudayl b. Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Salm al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from al-Hasan b. Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, who said: I heard Abu Hazim narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."
"2644","Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: al-Thawri informed us, from Salim b. Abi Hafsah, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."
"2645","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."
"2646","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym and Abu Ghassan Malik b. Ismail narrated to us, both saying: Isra'il narrated to us, saying: I heard Salim b. Abi Hafsah say: I heard Abu Hazim say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."
"2647","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Jumhur b. Mansur narrated to us: Sayf b. Muhammad narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: Whoever loves them, it is by my love; and whoever hates them, it is by hatred of me."
"2648","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb and Muhammad b. Umar al-Hayyaji narrated to us, (Ha). And Ali b. Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, both saying: Yahya b. Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated to us: Ubaydah b. al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim b. al-Walid al-Ta'i, from Talhah b. Musarrif, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves me has loved them - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."
"2649","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Maymun narrated to us: Ali b. Abis narrated to us, from Salim b. Abi Hafsah and Kathir al-Nawwa, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Allah, I love them, so love them, and hate whoever hates them."
"2650","Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. al-Hasan al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ahmad b. al-Walid b. Burd al-Antaki narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: al-Mutawakkil b. Musa narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Musri', from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the house of Fatimah and greeted; al-Hasan or al-Husayn came out to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Climb, may your father be sacrificed for you; you are the eye of a bug - holding him by his fingers - so he climbed onto his shoulder. Then the other, al-Hasan or al-Husayn, came out with one of his eyes raised, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Welcome to you; climb, may your father be sacrificed for you; you are the eye of the bug - and he held him by his fingers so he settled on his other shoulder. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held them by the backs of their necks until he placed their mouths upon his mouth, then said: O Allah, I love them, so love them and love whoever loves them."
"2651","Abdan b. Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us: Qutaybah b. Sa'id narrated to us: Hatim b. Isma'il narrated to us, from Muawiyah b. Abi Muzarrid, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: These two ears of mine heard and these two eyes of mine saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was holding with both his hands together Hasan or Husayn, with his feet upon the feet of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Huzuqqah, huzuqqah, climb, O eye of the bug; so the boy would climb until he placed his feet upon the chest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said to him: Open. Then he kissed him, then said: O Allah, love him, for I love him."
"2652","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Nasr b. Ali narrated to us: Ali b. Ja'far b. Muhammad narrated to us, from his brother Musa b. Ja'far, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali b. al-Husayn, from his father, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of al-Hasan and al-Husayn and said: Whoever loves these two, and their father and their mother, will be with me in my rank on the Day of Resurrection."
"2653","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Rustum, from Zadham, from Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Hasan and al-Husayn: Whoever loves them, I love him; whoever I love, Allah loves him; whoever Allah loves, He admits him to the Gardens of Bliss. And whoever hates them or wrongs them, I hate him; whoever I hate, Allah hates him; whoever Allah hates, He admits him to the punishment of Hell, and for him is a lasting punishment."
"2654","al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yusuf b. Salman al-Mazini narrated to us: Hatim b. Isma'il narrated to us: Sa'd b. Ishaq b. Ka'b b. Ujrah narrated to us, from Ishaq b. Abi Habibah, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Abu Hurayrah, that Marwan b. al-Hakam came to Abu Hurayrah in the illness in which he died, and Marwan said to Abu Hurayrah: I have held nothing against you since we kept company except your love of al-Hasan and al-Husayn. He said: So Abu Hurayrah braced himself and sat up, and said: I bear witness that we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until when we were on part of the road, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of al-Hasan and al-Husayn weeping while they were with their mother; so he hastened until he reached them, and I heard him say to her: What is the matter with my two sons? She said: Thirst. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back to a waterskin seeking water in it - and water that day was in puddles, and the people were seeking water - and he called out: Is there any of you who has water with him? And no one remained but turned with his hand to his waterskin seeking water in a skin, and none of them found a drop. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me one of them; so she handed him to him from beneath the curtain, and I saw the whiteness of her forearms when she handed him; he took him and pressed him to his chest while he was crying loudly without falling silent, so he stuck out his tongue for him and he began sucking it until he calmed down or became quiet, and I no longer heard him weeping, while the other kept weeping as before without falling silent. So he said: Hand me the other; so she handed him to him and he did likewise with him, and they both fell silent so I heard no sound from them. Then he said: Move on; so we spread out right and left away from the litters until we met him on the main road. So shall I not love these two when I have seen this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"2655","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla narrated to us: Ali b. Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: al-Husayn came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and clung to the neck of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he stood up with him and took him by the hand, and kept holding it until he bowed."
"2656","al-Hasan b. Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us: Khalid b. Yazid al-Urani narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus b. Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) part what was between the thighs of al-Husayn and kiss his zabibah."
"2657","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik b. Ismail narrated to us: Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: While we were praying the evening prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whenever he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, would leap onto his back; and when he wanted to bow, he would take them with his hand, taking gently, until he placed them on the ground; and when he returned they returned, until he finished his prayer and left, placing them on his thighs. Abu Hurayrah said: So I stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I take them away? He said: No. Then lightning flashed, and he said: Join your mother. And they remained in its light until they entered."
"2658","Muhammad b. Nasr b. Humayd al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Salih al-Azdi narrated to us: Musa b. Uthman al-Hadrami narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he loved him with intense love. He said: I am going to my mother. So I said: I shall go with him. Then lightning came from the sky, and he walked in its light until he reached."
"2659","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh b. al-Faraj and Ja'far b. Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, both saying: Yazid b. Mawhab al-Ramli narrated to us: Masruh Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was walking on all fours with al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, upon his back, saying: What an excellent camel your camel is, and what excellent riders you two are."
"2660","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Fudayl b. Marzuq narrated to us: Atiyyah al-Awfi narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from Umm Salamah, who said: This verse was revealed in my house: (Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly), while she was sitting at the door. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I not of the people of the House? He said: You are toward good."
"2661","Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us: Ja'far b. Musafir al-Tinnisi narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Musa b. Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, from Hashim b. Hashim, from Wahb b. Abdullah b. Zam'ah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered Fatimah, Hasan and Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them, then brought them under his garment, then said: O Allah, these are my Household. Umm Salamah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, admit me with them. He said: You are of my family."
"2662","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd b. Jud'an, from Shahr b. Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: Bring me your husband and your two sons. So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast a Fadak cloak, then placed his hand upon them, then said: O Allah, these are the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so place Your blessings and Your benedictions upon the family of Muhammad, for You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. Umm Salamah said: So I lifted the cloak to enter with them, but he pulled it from my hand and said: You are upon good."
"2663","Abd al-Warith b. Ibrahim Abu Ubaydah al-Askari narrated to us: Hawtharah b. Ashras al-Minqari narrated to us: Uqbah b. Abdullah al-Rifa'i narrated to us, from Shahr b. Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: Bring me your husband and your two sons. So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast a cloak over them, then said: O Allah, these are the family of Muhammad, so place Your blessings and Your benedictions upon the family of Muhammad as You placed them upon Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"2664","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us, (Ha). And Abu Khalifah al-Fadl b. al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Hamid b. Bahram al-Fazari narrated to us: Shahr b. Hawshab narrated to us, saying: I heard Umm Salamah say: Fatimah came in the morning with a tharid of hers, carrying it in a dish of hers until she placed it before him. He said to her: And where is the son of your uncle? She said: He is in the house. He said: Go, call him and bring me my two sons. So she came leading her two sons, each one in a hand, with Ali walking behind them, until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he seated them in his lap, Ali sat on his right, and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, sat on his left. Umm Salamah said: So I took from beneath me a cloak that was our mat upon the sleeping place in the house, with a pot in it containing khazirah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Call for me your husband and your two sons, al-Hasan and al-Husayn. So she called them, and they all sat eating from that pot. She said: And I was praying in that room, when this verse was revealed: (Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly). So he took the leftover of the cloak and covered them with it, then brought out his right hand from the cloak and pointed with it toward the sky, then said: O Allah, these are my Household and my close kin, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. Umm Salamah said: So I put my head into the house and said: O Messenger of Allah, and am I with you? He said: You are upon good - twice."
"2665","Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Hawdhah b. Khalifah narrated to us: Awf narrated to us, from Atiyyah Abu al-Mu'addil, from his father, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced Ali and Fatimah with one hand, and Hasan and Husayn with the other hand, draped over them a black khamisah that was upon him, kissed Ali and kissed Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with them both, then said: O Allah, to You, not to the Fire - I and my Household. Umm Salamah said: I said: And I? He said: And you."
"2666","Hafs b. Umar b. al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik b. Ismail narrated to us: Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik b. Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Umm Salamah, that Fatimah came with some food of hers to her father while he was on a sleeping place of his in the house of Umm Salamah. She said: He said: Go and call my two sons and the son of your uncle. So they came, and he covered them with a cloak, then said: O Allah, these are my Household and my close kin, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. Umm Salamah said: And am I with them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You are the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and toward - or upon - good."
"2667","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Abd al-Salam b. Harb narrated to us, from Kulthum b. Ziyad, from Abu Ammar, who said: I was sitting with Wathilah b. al-Asqa' when they mentioned Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and reviled him. When they stood up, he said: Sit until I inform you about this one whom they reviled. I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day when Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them, came; so he cast a cloak of his over them, then said: O Allah, these are my Household; O Allah, remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, and I? He said: And you. He said: By Allah, it is the most firmly relied-upon deed in my soul."
"2668","Muhammad b. Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us: Muhammad b. Bishr al-Tinnisi narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us: Abu Ammar Shaddad narrated to us, saying: Wathilah b. al-Asqa' al-Laythi said: I was intending to visit Ali but did not find him, so Fatimah said: He has gone to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to call him until he comes. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and he came; so I entered with them both. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Hasan and Husayn, seating each one of them upon his thigh, brought Fatimah close to his lap, then wrapped his garment over them while I was leaning back, then said: (Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly), then said: These are my family. Wathilah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and am I of your family? He said: And you are of my family. Wathilah said: It is the most hopeful thing I hope for."
"2669","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd b. Jud'an, from Anas b. Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by the house of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, for six months when he came out of the dawn prayer, saying: O people of the House, prayer - (Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly)."
"2670","Muhammad b. al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us: Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Mansur b. Abi al-Aswad say: I heard Abu Dawud say: I heard Abu al-Hamra say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to the door of Fatimah for six months, saying: (Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly)."
"2671","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Maymun narrated to us: Ali b. Abis narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, and from al-A'mash, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: This verse was revealed: (Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly) concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2672","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abayah b. Rib'i, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, most high, divided creation into two parts and placed me in the better of the two parts; that is His saying: (the companions of the right) and (the companions of the left) - so I am of the companions of the right, and I am of the best of the companions of the right. Then He made the two parts into houses and placed me in the better of the two houses; that is His saying: (Then the companions of the right - what are the companions of the right? And the companions of the left - what are the companions of the left? And the foremost, the foremost) - so I am of the best of the foremost. Then He made the houses into tribes and placed me in the best of them as a tribe; that is His saying: (peoples and tribes) - so I am the most God-fearing of the children of Adam and the most honored of them before Allah, mighty and majestic, and no boast. Then He made the tribes into houses and placed me in the best of them as a house; that is His saying: (Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly)."
"2673","Muhammad b. Ruzayq b. Jami' al-Misri narrated to us: al-Haytham b. Habib narrated to us: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali b. Ali al-Makki al-Hilali, from his father, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the illness in which he died, and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, was at his head. He said: So she wept until her voice rose; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his glance to her and said: My beloved Fatimah, what makes you weep? She said: I fear destitution after you. He said: O my beloved, did you not know that Allah, mighty and majestic, looked upon the earth with a look and chose from it your father, so he was sent with His message; then He looked with a look and chose from it your husband, and revealed to me that I should marry you to him. O Fatimah, we are a Household to whom Allah has given seven traits not given to anyone before us, nor to be given to anyone after us: I am the seal of the prophets, the most honored of the prophets before Allah, the most beloved of creation to Allah, mighty and majestic - and I am your father; my successor is the best of successors and the most beloved of them to Allah - and he is your husband; our martyr is the best of martyrs and the most beloved of them to Allah - and he is your uncle Hamzah b. Abd al-Muttalib, and he is the uncle of your father and the uncle of your husband; and from us is the one who has two green wings flying in Paradise with the angels wherever he wishes - and he is the son of your father's uncle and the brother of your husband; and from us are the two grandsons of this nation - and they are your two sons al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and they are the masters of the youth of Paradise, and their father, by the One who sent me with the truth, is better than them. O Fatimah, by the One who sent me with the truth, from them is the Mahdi of this nation when the world becomes tumult and confusion, trials multiply, roads are cut off, and some of them raid others - so no elder shows mercy to a younger, and no younger honors an elder; then Allah, mighty and majestic, will send at that time from them one who will open the fortresses of misguidance and wrapped hearts; he will uphold the religion at the end of time as I upheld it at the beginning of time, and will fill the world with justice as it was filled with injustice. O Fatimah, do not grieve and do not weep; for Allah, mighty and majestic, is more merciful to you and kinder to you than I, and that is because of your standing with me and your place in my heart; and Allah married you to your husband, who is the noblest of your household in lineage, the most honored of them in rank, the most merciful of them to subjects, the most just of them in equity, the most discerning of them in judgment. And I have asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, that you be the first of my Household to join me. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, did not remain after him except seventy-five days until Allah joined her to him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2674","Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Bara narrated to us: Abd al-Mun'im b. Idris b. Sinan narrated to us, from his father, from Wahb b. Munabbih, from Jabir b. Abdullah and Abdullah b. Abbas concerning the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: (When the help of Allah and the victory comes, and you see the people entering the religion of Allah in crowds, so glorify with the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is Accepting of repentance). He said: When it was revealed, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Jibril, my soul has been announced. Jibril, peace be upon him, said: The Hereafter is better for you than the first, and your Lord will give you and you will be pleased. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal to call out: prayer in congregation. So the Emigrants and Helpers gathered at the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah, mighty and majestic, and extolled Him, then delivered a sermon at which hearts trembled and eyes wept. Then he said: O people, what kind of prophet was I to you? They said: May Allah reward you from a prophet with good; you were to us like a merciful father, and like a sincere compassionate brother; you conveyed the messages of Allah, mighty and majestic, delivered to us His revelation, and called to the path of your Lord with wisdom and good admonition; so may Allah reward you on our behalf with the best He rewards a prophet on behalf of his nation. He said to them: O company of Muslims, I adjure you by Allah and by my right upon you: whoever has a wrong from me, let him stand and retaliate from me. No one stood up to him. So he adjured them a second time, and no one stood up to him. So he adjured them a third time: O company of Muslims, I adjure you by Allah and by my right upon you: whoever has a wrong from me, let him stand and retaliate from me before retaliation on the Resurrection. So an old shaykh called Ukashah stood up from among the Muslims and stepped over the Muslims until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; were it not that you adjured us time after time, I would not be one to venture upon anything of this. I was with you in a raid, and when Allah, mighty and majestic, gave us victory and aided His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we were on the return, my she-camel came alongside your she-camel, so I dismounted from the camel and drew near you to kiss your thigh; so you raised the stick and struck my side, and I do not know whether it was deliberate from you or you intended to strike the camel. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek refuge for you by the majesty of Allah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) should deliberately strike you. O Bilal, go to the house of Fatimah and bring me the unpeeled stick. So Bilal left the mosque with his hand upon the crown of his head, calling out: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving retaliation from himself. So he knocked at the door of Fatimah and said: O daughter of the Messenger of Allah, hand me the unpeeled stick. Fatimah said: O Bilal, what will my father do with the stick; this is neither a day of pilgrimage nor a day of battle? He said: O Fatimah, how unaware you are of what your father is in; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is bidding farewell to religion and leaving the world, and giving retaliation from himself. Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: O Bilal, who is it whose soul would be content to retaliate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? O Bilal, tell al-Hasan and al-Husayn to stand up to this man so he retaliates from them both, and not let him retaliate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Bilal entered the mosque and handed the stick to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed the stick to Ukashah. When Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, looked at that, they stood and said: O Ukashah, here we are before you, so retaliate from us and do not retaliate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Proceed, O Abu Bakr, and you, O Umar, proceed; for Allah has known your place and your standing. So Ali b. Abi Talib stood and said: O Ukashah, I am in life before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my soul is not content that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) be struck; here is my back and my belly, retaliate from me with your hand and flog me a hundred, and do not retaliate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, sit; for Allah, mighty and majestic, has known your standing and your intention. And al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, stood and said: O Ukashah, do you not know that we are the grandsons of the Messenger of Allah? So retaliation from us is like retaliation from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Sit, O delight of my eye; may Allah not forget for you both this standing. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ukashah, strike if you are striking. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you struck me while I was bare of my belly. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered his belly, and the Muslims cried out weeping and said: Do you think Ukashah will strike the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? When Ukashah looked at the whiteness of the belly of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as if white cotton cloth, he could not but fall upon it and kiss his belly, saying: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; whose soul could bear to retaliate from you? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Either strike, or pardon. He said: I have pardoned you, hoping that Allah will pardon me on the Resurrection. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to look at my companion in Paradise, let him look at this shaykh. So the Muslims stood and began kissing between the eyes of Ukashah, saying: Glad tidings to you, glad tidings to you; you have attained the highest ranks and the companionship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill from that day, remaining ill for eighteen days with the people visiting him. And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born on Monday, sent on Monday, and died on Monday. When it was Sunday he grew heavy in his illness, so Bilal called the call to prayer, then stood at the door and called: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, and the mercy of Allah; prayer, may Allah have mercy on you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of Bilal, so Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: O Bilal, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is today occupied with himself. So Bilal entered the mosque, and when dawn brightened, he said: By Allah, I shall not establish it unless I seek permission from my master, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he returned and stood at the door and called: Peace be upon you, O Messenger, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; prayer, may Allah have mercy on you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of Bilal and said: Enter, O Bilal; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is occupied with himself; order Abu Bakr to pray with the people. So he went out with his hand upon the crown of his head, saying: O succour of Allah, and severance of my hope, and breaking of my back; would that my mother had not borne me, and since she bore me, that I had not witnessed this day from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said: O Abu Bakr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) orders you to pray with the people. So Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stepped forward for the people - and he was a tender man - and when he looked at the emptiness of the place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he could not but fall unconscious, and the Muslims cried out weeping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the clamour of the people and said: What is this clamour? They said: The clamour of the Muslims at losing you, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ali b. Abi Talib and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and leaned upon them both, and went out to the mosque and prayed with the people two light units, then turned his handsome face to them and said: O company of Muslims, I entrust you to Allah; you are in the hope of Allah and His security, and Allah is my successor over you. O company of Muslims, upon you is fear of Allah and guarding obedience to Him after me, for I am leaving the world; this is the first day of the Hereafter and the last day of the days of the world. When it was Monday his affair grew severe, and Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed to the angel of death, peace be upon him, to descend to My beloved and My chosen, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in the best form, and be gentle with him in taking his soul. So the angel of death, peace be upon him, descended and stood at the door like a Bedouin, then said: Peace be upon you, O people of the house of prophethood, and mine of messengership, and frequentation of angels; may I enter? Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said to Fatimah: Answer the man. Fatimah said: May Allah reward your walking, O servant of Allah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is occupied with himself. So he called a second time, and Aisha said: O Fatimah, answer the man. Fatimah said: May Allah reward your walking, O servant of Allah; the Messenger is occupied with himself. Then he called a third time: Peace be upon you, O people of the house of prophethood, and mine of messengership, and frequentation of angels; may I enter? There is no escape from entering. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of the angel of death, peace be upon him, and said: O Fatimah, who is at the door? She said: O Messenger of Allah, a man at the door seeks permission to enter; we answered him time after time, then in the third he called with a voice at which my skin shivered and my limbs trembled. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O Fatimah, do you know who is at the door? This is the destroyer of pleasures, the separator of gatherings, the widower of wives, the orphaner of children, the ruiner of houses, the builder of graves; this is the angel of death, peace be upon him. Enter, may Allah have mercy on you, O angel of death. So the angel of death entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O angel of death, have you come to me as a visitor or as a taker? He said: I have come to you as a visitor and a taker, and Allah, mighty and majestic, ordered me not to enter upon you except by your permission, and not to take your soul except by your permission; if you permit, and otherwise I shall return to my Lord, mighty and majestic. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O angel of death, where did you leave my beloved Jibril? He said: I left him in the lowest heaven with the angels consoling him concerning you. It was not swifter than that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and sat at his head. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Jibril, this is the departure from the world, so give me glad tidings of what is for me with Allah. He said: I give you glad tidings, O beloved of Allah, that I have left the doors of heaven opened, and the angels standing in rows upon rows with greeting and sweet basil greeting your soul, O Muhammad. He said: Praise be to the face of my Lord; and give me glad tidings, O Jibril. He said: I give you glad tidings that the doors of the gardens have been opened, their rivers made to flow, their trees lowered, and their houris adorned for the coming of your soul, O Muhammad. He said: Praise be to the face of my Lord; so give me glad tidings, O Jibril. He said: You are the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted on the Resurrection. He said: Praise be to the face of my Lord. Jibril said: O my beloved, about what are you asking me? He said: I ask you about my worry and my concern: who is for the reciters of the Quran after me? Who is for the fasting of the month of Ramadan after me? Who is for the pilgrims of the sacred House of Allah after me? Who is for my chosen nation after me? He said: Rejoice, O beloved of Allah, for Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Paradise has been forbidden to all prophets and nations until you and your nation enter it, O Muhammad. He said: Now my soul is content; then, O angel of death, proceed to what you were ordered. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, when you are taken, who will wash you? In what shall we shroud you? Who will pray over you? Who will enter the grave? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, as for washing, you wash me, and al-Fadl b. Abbas will pour water upon you, and Jibril, peace be upon him, is your third; when you finish washing me, shroud me in three new garments, and Jibril, peace be upon him, will bring me embalming from Paradise; when you place me upon the bier, place me in the mosque and go out from me, for the first to pray over me is the Lord, mighty and majestic, from above His throne, then Jibril, peace be upon him, then Mika'il, then Israfil, peace be upon them both, then the angels in groups upon groups; then enter and stand in rows with none preceding over me. Fatimah, may Allah, most high, be pleased with her, said: Today is separation; when shall I meet you? He said to her: O my daughter, you will meet me on the Day of Resurrection at the Basin while I give drink to whoever comes to me at the Basin from my nation. She said: If I do not meet you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You will meet me at the Scale while I intercede for my nation. She said: If I do not meet you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You will meet me at the Bridge while I call: My Lord, save my nation from the Fire. So the angel of death, peace be upon him, drew near treating the taking of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when the soul reached the knees, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Oh. When the soul reached the navel, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: O distress. Fatimah, peace be upon her, said: My distress, O my father. When the soul reached the collarbone, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: O Jibril, how severe is the bitterness of death. So Jibril, peace be upon him, turned his face away from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Jibril, did you dislike looking at me? Jibril, peace be upon him, said: O my beloved, whose soul could bear to look at you while you treat the agonies of death? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken; Ali b. Abi Talib washed him, Ibn Abbas poured water upon him, and Jibril, peace be upon him, was with them both; he was shrouded in three new garments and carried upon a bier. Then they brought him into the mosque, placed him in the mosque, and the people went out from him; the first to pray over him was the Lord, most high, from above His throne, then Jibril, then Mika'il, then Israfil, then the angels in groups upon groups. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We heard in the mosque a humming and did not see for them a person; we heard a caller calling and saying: Enter, may Allah have mercy on you, and pray over your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So we entered and stood in rows upon rows as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us; we magnified with the magnification of Jibril, peace be upon him, and prayed over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the prayer of Jibril, peace be upon him, with none of us preceding over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Ali b. Abi Talib and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, entered the grave, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was buried. When the people left, Fatimah said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: O Abu al-Hasan, did you bury the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: How could your souls bear to throw dust upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Was there no mercy for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in your breasts; was he not the teacher of good? He said: Yes, O Fatimah, but the decree of Allah which none repels. So she began weeping and lamenting, saying: O my father, now Jibril, peace be upon him, is cut off; and Jibril used to come to us with revelation from heaven."
"2675","al-Husayn b. Muhammad al-Hannat al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us: Ahmad b. Rushd b. Khaytham al-Hilali narrated to us: my uncle Sa'id b. Khaytham narrated to us: Muslim al-Mula'i narrated to us, from Habbah al-Urani and Abu al-Bakhtari, from Salman, who said: We were around the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when Umm Ayman came and said: O Messenger of Allah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn have been lost. He said: And that was at mid-morning - meaning the rising of the day - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand and seek my two sons. He said: And each man took the direction of his face, and I took toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he kept going until he reached the foot of a mountain, and there were al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, each one clinging to his companion, with a serpent standing upon its tail, with something like fire coming out of its mouth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened to it; it turned addressing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then slipped away and entered some of the rocks. Then he came to them, separated them, wiped their faces, and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you both; how honored you are before Allah. Then he carried one of them upon his right shoulder and the other upon his left shoulder. So I said: Glad tidings to you both; what an excellent mount your mount is. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what excellent riders they are, and their father is better than them."
"2676","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Minjab b. al-Harith narrated to us: Ali b. Mushir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik b. Abi Sulayman, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, I am leaving among you that which, if you hold to it, you will never go astray after me - two matters, one of them greater than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope extended between heaven and earth; and my progeny, my Household; and they will never separate until they come to me at the Basin."
"2677","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Salih narrated to us: Salih b. Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, in a raised narration, who said: As if I have been called and answered; I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah, a rope extended between heaven and earth; and my progeny, my Household; and they will never separate until they come to me at the Basin. So look at how you succeed me concerning them."
"2678","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Nasr b. Abd al-Rahman al-Washsha narrated to us: Zayd b. al-Hasan al-Anmati narrated to us, from Ja'far b. Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his pilgrimage on the day of Arafah while he was upon his she-camel al-Qaswa; he addressed, and I heard him saying: O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my progeny, my Household."
"2679","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ja'far b. Humayd narrated to us: Abdullah b. Bukayr al-Ghanawi narrated to us, from Hakim b. Jubayr, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Zayd b. Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am a forerunner for you, and you will come to me at the Basin, its width what is between San'a and Busra, in it the number of stars of cups of gold and silver. So look at how you succeed me concerning the two weighty things. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the two weighty things? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The greater is the Book of Allah - a cause, one end of which is in the hand of Allah and the other end in your hands; so hold fast to it, you will never cease, and never go astray. And the smaller is my progeny; and they will never separate until they come to me at the Basin. And I asked my Lord that for them both; so do not precede them lest you perish, and do not teach them, for they are more knowledgeable than you."
"2680","Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Irs al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad b. Muhammad al-Yamami narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the afternoon prayer; when he was in the fourth, al-Hasan and al-Husayn came until they rode upon the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he placed them before him. And al-Husayn came forward, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried al-Hasan upon his right shoulder and al-Husayn upon his left shoulder, then said: O people, shall I not inform you of the best of people in grandfather and grandmother? Shall I not inform you of the best of people in paternal uncle and paternal aunt? Shall I not inform you of the best of people in maternal uncle and maternal aunt? Shall I not inform you of the best of people in father and mother? They are al-Hasan and al-Husayn: their grandfather is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), their grandmother is Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, their mother is Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), their father is Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, their paternal uncle is Ja'far b. Abi Talib, their paternal aunt is Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, their maternal uncle is al-Qasim, son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and their maternal aunts are Zaynab, Ruqayyah and Umm Kulthum, daughters of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Their grandfather is in Paradise, their father is in Paradise, their uncle is in Paradise, their aunt is in Paradise, their maternal aunts are in Paradise, they two are in Paradise, and whoever loves them is in Paradise."
"2681","Muhammad b. al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to us, (Ha). And Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami and Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, both saying: Nasr b. Abd al-Rahman al-Washsha narrated to us: Zayd b. al-Hasan al-Anmati narrated to us: Ma'ruf b. Kharrabudh narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah b. Asid al-Ghifari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, I am a forerunner for you, and you will come to me at the Basin - a basin wider than what is between San'a and Busra, in it the number of stars of cups of silver. And I shall ask you, when you come to me, about the two weighty things; so look at how you succeed me concerning them: the greater cause is the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic - a cause, one end of which is in the hand of Allah and the other end in your hands; so hold fast to it, and do not go astray nor alter. And my progeny, my Household; for the Subtle, the Aware has informed me that they will never end until they come to me at the Basin."
"2682","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Juhadah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Duba'i, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Book has been lifted, the Pen has dried, and matters decreed in a Book that has passed."
"2683","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali b. al-Hasan, from his grandmother, that al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to practice withdrawal from her, and she was his concubine."
"2684","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Jahsh, from Muawiyah b. Qurrah, from al-Hasan b. Ali, that he was asked about cheese and said: Put the knife, mention Allah's name, and eat."
"2685","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu al-Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Shu'bah, who said: I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, circumambulate after the afternoon prayer and pray two units."
"2686","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ali b. al-Mundhir al-Tariqi narrated to us: Uthman b. Sa'id al-Zayyat narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah Abu Raja al-Habati al-Tustari narrated to us: Shu'bah b. al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, asked his son al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about matters of manliness, saying: O my son, what is uprightness? He said: O my father, uprightness is repelling evil with good. He said: What is honor? He said: Benefiting one's clan, bearing others' offenses, agreeing with brothers, and guarding neighbours. He said: What is manliness? He said: Chastity, and managing wealth well. He said: What is exactness? He said: Looking into small matters, and withholding trifles. He said: What is blame? He said: A man guarding himself, and offering his wife. He said: What is generosity? He said: Giving from hardship and ease. He said: What is miserliness? He said: To consider what you spent as lost. He said: What is brotherhood? He said: Consoling in hardship and ease. He said: What is cowardice? He said: Boldness toward a friend, and holding back from an enemy. He said: What is gain? He said: Desire for God-consciousness, and asceticism in the world - it is the cool gain. He said: What is forbearance? He said: Swallowing anger, and mastering the soul. He said: What is wealth? He said: Contentment of the soul with what Allah, most high, apportioned for it, even if little; wealth is only wealth of the soul. He said: What is poverty? He said: Greed of the soul for everything. He said: What is defensibility? He said: Severity of might, and contending with the mightiest of people. He said: What is humiliation? He said: Panic at a believed report. He said: What is dullness? He said: Playing with the beard, and much spitting when addressing. He said: What is boldness? He said: Agreeing with peers. He said: What is affectation? He said: Your speaking about what does not concern you. He said: What is glory? He said: To give despite indebtedness, and to pardon offenses. He said: What is intellect? He said: Guarding the heart whatever you entrust it with. He said: What is folly? He said: Opposing your imam, and raising your speech over him. He said: What is good praise? He said: Doing good and abandoning evil. He said: What is resolve? He said: Long deliberation, and gentleness with rulers. He said: What is foolishness? He said: Following baseness, and accompanying the misguided. He said: What is heedlessness? He said: Abandoning the mosque, and obeying the corrupter. He said: What is deprivation? He said: Abandoning your share when it is offered to you. He said: What is the corrupter? He said: A fool with his wealth, negligent with his honor. Then Ali said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No poverty is severer than ignorance, no wealth returns more than intellect, no solitude is lonelier than conceit, no support succeeds more than consultation, no intellect is like planning, no lineage is like good character, no scrupulousness is like restraint, no worship is like reflection, no faith is like modesty and patience; the bane of speech is lying, the bane of knowledge is forgetting, the bane of forbearance is foolishness, the bane of worship is languor, the bane of refinement is insolence, the bane of courage is transgression, the bane of generosity is reminding, the bane of beauty is vanity, and the bane of lineage is boasting. O my son, never belittle any man you see: if he is better than you, consider him your father; if he is like you, he is your brother; and if he is younger than you, consider him your son. Abu al-Qasim said: None narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Muhammad b. Abdullah Abu Raja al-Habati; Uthman b. Sa'id al-Zayyat is alone in it, and it is not narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except with this chain."
"2687","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Nusayr b. Dhu'luq, from Muslim b. Iyad, who said: I asked al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the two units of Friday, and he said: They make up for what is besides them."
"2688","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus b. Ubayd, from al-Hasan, who said: Ziyad used to pursue the partisans of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, killing them; that reached al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, so he said: O Allah, single him out with death; for killing is expiation."
"2689","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. al-Hakam b. Abi Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sufyan b. Uyaynah, from Ubaydullah b. Abdullah b. al-Asamm, from his uncle Yazid b. al-Asamm, who said: I went out with al-Hasan, while a slave girl was scraping something of henna from his nails; a bundle of letters came to him, so he said: O slave girl, bring the dye vessel. So she poured water in it, and he cast the letters into the water; he did not open any of them nor look at it. So I said: O Abu Muhammad, from whom are these letters? He said: From the people of Iraq - a people who neither return to truth nor fall short of falsehood. I do not fear them for myself, but I fear them for that one - and he pointed to al-Husayn."
"2690","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sufyan b. Uyaynah, from Raqabah b. Masqalah, who said: When al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was dying, he said: Take me out to the open land, perhaps I may look upon the kingdom of the heavens - meaning the signs. When he was taken out, he said: O Allah, I commend my soul to You, for it is the dearest of souls to me. And among what Allah did for him was that he commended his soul."
"2691","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, died at the age of forty-seven."
"2692","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us: Yahya b. Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr b. Hafs, that Sa'd and al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, died in the time of Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, and they think that he poisoned him."
"2693","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, died in the year forty-nine, in the month of Rabi' al-Awwal."
"2694","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh b. al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us: Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, died in the year forty-nine; Sa'id b. al-As prayed over him; his death was in Madinah at the age of forty-six or forty-seven."
"2695","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim b. Adawiyyah narrated to us: Shurahbil narrated to me, saying: I was with al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when the bier of al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought out; he intended to bury him with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), fearing that Banu Umayyah would prevent him. When they reached the mosque with him, Banu Umayyah stood up; so Abdullah b. Ja'far stood and said: I heard him say: If they prevent you, bury me with my mother."
"2696","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Muhammad b. Bashshar Bundar narrated to us: Abd al-Malik b. al-Sabbah al-Misma'i narrated to us: Imran b. Hudayr narrated to us - I think from Abu Mijlaz - who said: Amr b. al-As and al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said to Muawiyah: al-Hasan b. Ali is tongue-tied, though he has speech and opinion; he has known his speech, so he will speak speech and find no speech. He said: Do not do it. But they insisted upon him. So Amr ascended the pulpit, mentioned Ali and attacked him. Then al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah ascended, praised Allah and extolled Him, then attacked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Then it was said to al-Hasan b. Ali: Ascend. He said: I shall neither ascend nor speak until you grant me that if I speak truth you will confirm me, and if I speak falsehood you will belie me. So they granted him; he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: By Allah, O Amr, and you, O Mughirah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the driver and the rider, one of them so-and-so? They said: O Allah, yes, indeed. He said: I adjure you by Allah, O Muawiyah and O Mughirah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed Amr with a curse for every rhyme he uttered? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, O Amr, and you, O Muawiyah b. Abi Sufyan, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the people of this one? They said: Yes. al-Hasan said: I praise Allah who - you attacked one who is free of this. And he mentioned the hadith."
"2697","Muhammad b. Awn al-Sirafi narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Ali al-Wasiti narrated to us: Yazid b. Harun narrated to us: Hariz b. Uthman informed us, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Awf, who said: Amr b. al-As and Abu al-A'war al-Sulami said to Muawiyah: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, is a tongue-tied man. Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Do not say that; for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in his mouth, and one in whose mouth the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat is not tongue-tied. al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: As for you, O Amr, two men disputed concerning you, so look which of them is your father; and as for you, O Abu al-A'war, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed Ri'l, Dhakwan and Amr b. Sufyan."
"2698","What al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, transmitted; A'ishah from al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with them both: Ali b. Sa'id b. Bashir al-Razi narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Hasan b. Ali b. Shahriyar al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abdullah b. Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Isma'il b. Ibrahim b. Uqbah narrated to me, from his uncle Musa b. Uqbah, from Hisham b. Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the supplication of qunut in witr: O Allah, guide us among those You guided, grant us well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend us among those You befriended, bless for us in what You gave, and protect us from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You, and indeed none whom You befriend is humbled; blessed and exalted are You."
"2699","Abu al-Hawra from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Ahmad b. Ishaq b. Wadih al-Assal al-Misri narrated to us: Sa'id b. Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, from Musa b. Uqbah, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to say in witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed none whom You befriend is humbled, and none whom You oppose is honored; blessed and exalted are You."
"2700","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: al-Hakam b. Marwan narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, who said: It was said to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: What did you memorize from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I memorized from him only words I say in witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted."
"2701","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Ali b. Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, (Ha). And Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah and Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, all saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: My grandfather, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), taught me words I say in witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed none whom You befriend is humbled, and none whom You oppose is honored; blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted."
"2702","Muhammad b. Amr b. Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah, most high, be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; none whom You befriend is humbled, and none whom You oppose is honored; blessed and exalted are You."
"2703","al-Hasan b. al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Affan b. Muslim narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me words I say in the qunut of witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed none whom You befriend is humbled, and none whom You oppose is honored; blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted."
"2704","Hashim b. Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us: Abu Salih al-Farra narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to say these words in witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You, and none whom You befriend is humbled; blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted."
"2705","Muhammad b. Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us: Amr b. Marzuq narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, who said: I heard al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to say in witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, befriend me among those You befriended, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed none whom You befriend is humbled, and none whom You oppose is honored; blessed and exalted are You."
"2706","Hashim b. Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us: Abu Salih al-Farra narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Hasan b. Ubaydullah, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, who said: I said to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: Of what age were you in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And what did you retain from him? He said: I retained from him that I heard him say: Leave what puts you in doubt for what does not put you in doubt; for evil is doubt, and good is tranquility. And I retained from him the five prayers, and words I say at their conclusion. He said: Say: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed none whom You befriend is humbled; blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted. Burayd b. Abi Maryam said: So I entered upon Muhammad b. Ali in al-Shi'b and narrated to him this hadith from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: He spoke the truth; they are words he taught us to say in qunut."
"2707","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Amr b. Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: al-Ala b. Salih narrated to us, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, who said: I said to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: What did you memorize from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The five prayers."
"2708","Ahmad b. al-Qasim b. Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, who said: I said to al-Hasan b. Ali: What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I remember from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I took a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed it with its saliva and put it among the dates. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it to you from this date for this boy? He said: We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us."
"2709","Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Hasan b. Umarah: Burayd b. Abi Maryam narrated to me, from Abu al-Hawra, who said: I said to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Of what age were you on the day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died? And what do you retain from him? He said: I retained from him that a man came to him one day and asked him about something, and he said: Leave what puts you in doubt for what does not put you in doubt; for evil is doubt, and good is tranquility. And I retained from him that I passed by him one day while before him in a heap of the heaps of charity dates; so I took a date and put it in my mouth; so he seized my neck, then put his hand in my mouth and pulled it out with its saliva, then threw it in the heap. His companions said to him: Had you left the boy to eat it? He said: Charity is not lawful for the family of Muhammad. He said: And he taught me words with which I supplicate at the end of qunut: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, befriend me among those You befriended, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You, and indeed none whom You befriend is humbled; blessed and exalted are You."
"2710","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. al-Nu'man al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us: Sufyan b. Waki' b. al-Jarrah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Yunus b. Abi Ishaq, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam al-Saluli, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me words I say in the qunut of witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; for indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed none whom You befriend is humbled; blessed and exalted are You."
"2711","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us: al-Rabi' b. Sahl Abu Ibrahim al-Fazari narrated to us: al-Rabi' b. al-Rukayn narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Zarrad, from Abu al-Hawra, who said: I met al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, at Basrah and said: May my soul be for you, what did you memorize from your father Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He taught me words I say in witr. I said: What are they? He said: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me in what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You. I said: May my soul be for you, did you memorize from him other than this? He said: I was walking with him in a garden of charity, so I took a date and put it in my mouth; so he put his hand in until he took it out, and said: O my son, did you not know that we, the people of the House, charity is not lawful for us?"
"2712","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Tahir b. Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: my father narrated to us: al-Ala b. Salih narrated to us, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, who said: We were with al-Hasan b. Ali when he was asked: What did you retain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I was walking with him one day, and he passed by a threshing floor of charity dates; so I found a date and put it in my mouth; so he took it out with my saliva. Some of the people said: What is it to you, O Messenger of Allah, had you left it? He said: We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us."
"2713","Abu Wa'il Shaqiq b. Salamah from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ja'far b. Humayd narrated to us: Hudayj b. Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Shaqiq b. Salamah, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two sons of hers; so he gave her three dates; she gave her two sons, each one of them a date; they ate their two dates, then began looking at their mother; so she split her date in halves between them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has shown her mercy because of her mercy to her two sons."
"2714","Amir al-Sha'bi from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: Abu al-Zinba' Rawh b. al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us: Yahya b. Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us: Ahmad b. Bishr narrated to us: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while in his hand was a bone he was gnawing from. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and bit from it a bite or two, then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"2715","Hubayrah b. Yarim from al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him: Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: Yahya b. Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us: Yazid b. Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, that al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed the people, saying: O people, you have lost a man whom neither the first ones preceded nor the last ones will reach. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him on expeditions, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left; by Allah, he left neither white nor yellow except eight hundred dirhams for the price of a servant."
"2716","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ali b. Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from al-Hasan b. Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him on expeditions - meaning Ali, may Allah be pleased with him - so he would fight, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left, and he would not return until Allah gave him victory."
"2717","Mahmud b. Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Wahb b. Baqiyyah narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, who said: I heard al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressing the people, saying: O people, yesterday a man left you whom neither the first ones preceded in knowledge, nor will the last ones reach. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him on a mission, giving him the banner, and he would not return until Allah gave him victory; Jibril was on his right and Mika'il on his left. He left neither yellow nor white except seven hundred dirhams with which he intended to buy a servant."
"2718","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Dirar b. Surad narrated to us: Yahya b. Ya'la narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from al-Hasan b. Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not send Ali on any mission except giving him the banner."
"2719","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Dirar b. Surad narrated to us: Ali b. Hashim narrated to us, from Sadaqah b. Abi Imran, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never sent Ali on a mission except giving him the banner."
"2720","Musa b. Harun and Muhammad b. al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, both saying: Isa b. Salim al-Shashi narrated to us: Ubaydullah b. Amr narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man has left you whom none of the first ones preceded in knowledge, nor will any of the last ones reach. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him, giving him the banner; then he would go out and not return until Allah, mighty and majestic, gave him victory, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left fighting with him. He died leaving neither dinar nor dirham, except ornaments worth seven hundred dirhams remaining from his stipend."
"2721","Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Muhammad b. Kathir narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man has left you who left neither yellow nor white except seven hundred dirhams from his stipend with which he intended to buy a servant - meaning Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2722","Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: Isma'il b. Zakariyya al-Kufi narrated to us: Ali b. Abis narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, who said: al-Hasan addressed, saying: Yesterday a man left you whom neither the first ones preceded in knowledge nor will the last ones reach. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him on a mission, giving him the banner, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left; he would not return until Allah, mighty and majestic, gave him victory."
"2723","al-Hasan b. Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us: Sa'id b. Ufayr narrated to us: Bakkar b. Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, that when Ali, may Allah, most high, be pleased with him, died, al-Hasan b. Ali stood upon the pulpit and said: O people, tonight a man has been taken among you whom neither the first ones preceded nor will the last ones reach. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him on missions, with Jibril encompassing him on his right and Mika'il on his left; he would not turn back until victory was given to them. He left only seven hundred dirhams with which he intended to buy a servant. And he was taken on the night in which Isa son of Maryam was raised - the night of the twenty-seventh of Ramadan."
"2724","Muawiyah b. Hudayj from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Amr al-Waqifi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Yazid, from Muawiyah b. Hudayj, who said: Muawiyah b. Abi Sufyan, may Allah have mercy on him, sent me to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, to propose on behalf of Yazid for a daughter or a sister of his. So I came to him and mentioned Yazid to him, and he said: We are a people whose women are not married until we consult them; so go to her. So I came to her and mentioned Yazid to her, and she said: By Allah, that shall not be until your companion marches among us as Pharaoh marched among the Children of Israel, slaughtering their sons and sparing their women. So I returned to al-Hasan and said: You sent me to a piece of calamity who calls the Commander of the Believers Pharaoh. He said: O Muawiyah, beware of hating us; for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None hates us or envies us except he will be driven on the Day of Resurrection with whips of fire."
"2725","Abu Kabir from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us, (Ha). And Abd al-Rahman b. Salm al-Razi narrated to us, both saying: Abbad b. Ya'qub al-Asadi narrated to us: Ali b. Abis narrated to us, from Badr b. al-Khalil Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Kabir, who said: I was sitting with al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when a man came to him and said: A man called Muawiyah - meaning Ibn Hudayj - reviled Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, with foul reviling in the presence of Muawiyah; do you know him? He said: Yes. He said: When you see him, bring him to me. He said: So he saw him at the house of Amr b. Hurayth and pointed him out to him. He said: Are you Muawiyah b. Hudayj? He remained silent and did not answer him three times. Then he said: Are you the one who reviles Ali in the presence of the son of the eater of livers? Were you to come to him at the Basin - and I do not think you will come to it - you would find him with sleeves rolled up, forearms bare, driving the disbelievers and hypocrites away from the Basin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as strange camels are driven away from their owner - the saying of the truthful, the believed, Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2726","Al-Musayyab b. Najabah from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ibrahim b. al-Hasan al-Taghlibi narrated to us: Ubaydullah b. Bukayr al-Ghanawi narrated to us, from Hakim b. Jubayr, from Abu Idris, from al-Musayyab b. Najabah, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit."
"2727","Hasan b. Hasan b. Ali from his father, may Allah be pleased with him: Ahmad b. Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us: Sa'id b. Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us: Humayd b. Abi Zaynab informed me, from Hasan b. Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wherever you are, send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me."
"2728","Ibrahim b. Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us: Kathir b. Yahya narrated to us: Hafs b. Umar al-Raqqashi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Hasan b. Hasan b. Ali narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when people come to the house and one of them seeks permission, does it suffice for all of them? He said: Yes. It was said: When a man of the people returns greeting, does it suffice for all? He said: Yes. It was said: When people pass and one of them gives greeting, does it suffice for all? He said: Yes. It was said: When a man of the people returns it, does it suffice for all? He said: Yes."
"2729","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abbadah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Ya'qub b. Muhammad narrated to us: Jahm b. Uthman narrated to us, from Abdullah b. Hasan b. Hasan, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the necessitators of forgiveness is bringing joy to your Muslim brother."
"2730","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Abdah b. Abdullah narrated to us: Qays b. Muhammad al-Kindi narrated to us: Talhah b. Kamil narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Hisham, from Abdullah b. al-Hasan, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cheated one is neither praised nor rewarded."
"2731","Ibrahim b. Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us: Kathir b. Yahya narrated to us: Hafs b. Umar al-Raqqashi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Hasan b. Hasan narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the Verse of the Throne after the prescribed prayer will be in the protection of Allah until the next prayer."
"2732","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Musarrif b. Amr al-Yami narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. Talhah narrated to us, from his father, from Yasin al-Zayyat Abu Mu'adh, from Abu Abdullah al-Makki, from Abdullah b. al-Hasan b. al-Hasan, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed while men and women were circumambulating before him without a barrier, on the side of the Black Stone."
"2733","Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith b. Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us: Muhammad b. Jami' al-Attar narrated to us: Fadalah b. Husayn narrated to us: a man of the people of Madinah, kunya Abu Abdullah, narrated to me: Abdullah b. Hasan b. Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Date palms and trees are a blessing for their owners and for their descendants after them, when they are grateful to Allah."
"2734","Ahmad b. Muhammad al-Nakha'i al-Qadi al-Kufi narrated to us: Ammar b. Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Abdullah b. Hasan b. Hasan, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sacrifices with a content soul, seeking reward for his sacrifice, it will be a veil for him from the Fire."
"2735","Ahmad b. al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us: Ahmad b. al-Nu'man al-Farra al-Massisi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Uthman al-Hatibi narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah b. Muhammad al-Juhani, from Abdullah b. al-Hasan b. Ali, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit on the day of the Tabuk expedition, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, by Allah, I command you only with what Allah commanded you, and forbid you only from what Allah forbade you. So seek livelihood gracefully; by the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, your provision seeks you as your term seeks you. If something of it becomes difficult for you, seek it through obedience to Allah, mighty and majestic."
"2736","Musa b. Jumhur al-Tinnisi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Musaffa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Jahm b. Uthman narrated to me, from Abdullah b. Hasan b. Hasan, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the necessitators of forgiveness is your bringing joy to your Muslim brother."
"2737","Zayd b. Ali from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Salim narrated to us: Husayn b. Zayd b. Ali narrated to us, from al-Hasan b. Zayd, from his father, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when performing ablution would leave extra water until he let it flow upon the place of his prostration."
"2738","Abu Yahya al-A'raj from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal al-Anmati narrated to us, (Ha). And Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, both saying: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ata b. al-Sa'ib, from Abu Yahya, who said: I was between al-Hasan and al-Husayn while Marwan and they were reviling one another; al-Hasan kept silencing al-Husayn. Marwan said: A cursed household. So al-Hasan became angry and said: You said a cursed household; by Allah, Allah cursed you upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while you were in the backbone of your father."
"2739","Rabi'ah b. Shayban from al-Hasan b. Ali: Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Waki' and Abu Usamah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us, from Thabit b. Umarah, from Rabi'ah b. Shayban, who said: I said to al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: What do you retain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I went up with him to the charity storeroom, took a date and chewed it; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Throw it; for charity is not lawful for us."
"2740","Ishaq b. Yasar, Abu Muhammad b. Ishaq, from al-Hasan b. Ali: Muhammad b. Abdus b. Kamil al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Amr b. Aban narrated to us: Muhammad b. Fudayl narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from his father, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the house of Fatimah; she handed him a cooked shoulder of sheep, so he ate it, then stood to pray. She took his clothes and said: Will you not perform ablution, O Messenger of Allah? He said: From what, O my daughter? She said: You ate of what fire touched. He said: The purest of your food is what fire touched."
"2741","Muhammad b. Sirin from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Muhammad b. Sirin, that al-Hasan b. Ali and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, were sitting when a funeral passed; one of them stood and the other did not stand. One of them said: Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand? The other said: Yes, then he sat."
"2742","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad b. Sirin, who said: A funeral passed by Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both; al-Hasan stood and Ibn Abbas sat. al-Hasan said: Did not the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand for a funeral of a Jew or Jewess that passed by him? Ibn Abbas said: Yes, and he sat."
"2743","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Hammad al-Shu'aythi narrated to us: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, that a funeral passed over Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both; one of them stood and the other sat. The standing one said to the sitting one: Did not the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand? He said: Yes, then he sat."
"2744","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Nu'man b. Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Sa'd b. Abd al-Rahman, Yazid b. Ibrahim al-Tustari and Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, all saying: Muhammad b. Sirin narrated to us, saying: I was informed that al-Hasan b. Ali and Ibn Abbas - a funeral passed over them both; al-Hasan stood and Ibn Abbas sat. al-Hasan said to Ibn Abbas: Did you not see that a funeral passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he stood? He said: Yes, and he sat."
"2745","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Shu'ayb al-Rajjani narrated to us: Yahya b. Hakim al-Muqawwim narrated to us: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us: Ash'ath narrated to us, from Muhammad, that Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, were sitting when a funeral passed by them both; al-Hasan stood and Ibn Abbas sat. He said: Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and sat?"
"2746","Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, that al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Had you looked from Jabars to Jabalq, you would not find a man whose grandfather is a prophet other than me and my brother. And I think you should gather upon Muawiyah: (And I do not know; perhaps it is a trial for you and enjoyment for a time). Ma'mar said: Jabars and Jabalq are the east and the west."
"2747","Abu Layla from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Layla, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Anas, go and call for me the master of the Arabs - meaning Ali. A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: Are you not the master of the Arabs? He said: I am the master of the children of Adam, and Ali is the master of the Arabs. When Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to the Helpers, so they came to him. He said to them: O company of Helpers, shall I not guide you to that which, if you hold to it, you will never go astray after it? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This is Ali, so love him for my love, and honor him for my honor; for Jibril, peace be upon him, ordered me with what I said to you from Allah, mighty and majestic."
"2748","Umayr b. Ma'mun from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad b. al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to us: Marwan b. Muawiyah narrated to us, from Sa'd b. Tarif, from Umayr b. Ma'mun, who said: I heard al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I heard my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: Whoever habitually frequents the mosque attains a brother gained for the sake of Allah, mighty and majestic, and beneficial knowledge, and a word calling him to guidance, and a word turning him away from ruin, and abandons sins out of modesty or fear, and an awaited blessing or mercy."
"2749","al-Qasim b. Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Sa'd b. Tarif, from Umayr b. Ma'mun, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gift of the fasting person is oil and incense."
"2750","Habib b. Abi Thabit from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Allan b. Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us: Umar b. Muhammad b. al-Hasan narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Hammad b. Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, from al-Hasan b. Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did each: he entered ihram when his mount stood straight with him, and he entered ihram while in al-Bayda on the ground before his mount stood straight with him."
"2751","Umm Unays bint al-Hasan b. Ali from her father: al-Abbas b. Hamdan al-Asbahani narrated to us: Shu'ayb b. Abd al-Hamid al-Tahhan narrated to us: Yazid b. Harun narrated to us: Shayban informed us, from al-Hakam b. Abdullah b. Khattaf, from Umm Unays bint al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, from her father, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: (Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet)? He said: This is of the concealed; were it not that you asked me about it, I would not inform you. Allah, mighty and majestic, entrusted me with two angels: I am never mentioned before a Muslim servant and he sends blessings upon me except those two angels say: May Allah forgive you; and Allah and His angels say in answer to those two angels: Amen. And none sends blessings upon me except those two angels say: May Allah forgive you; and Allah and His angels say in answer to those two angels: Amen."
"2752","Yusuf b. Mazin al-Rasibi from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar and al-Abbas b. Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, both saying: Zayd b. Akhzam narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: al-Qasim b. al-Fadl narrated to us, from Yusuf b. Mazin al-Rasibi, who said: A man stood up to al-Hasan b. Ali and said: You blackened the faces of the believers. He said: Do not blame me, may Allah have mercy on you; for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shown Banu Umayyah addressing upon his pulpit, man after man, and that grieved him. So this verse was revealed: (Indeed We gave you al-Kawthar) - a river in Paradise. And revealed: (Indeed We sent it down in the Night of Decree. And what will make you know what the Night of Decree is? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months) - which Banu Umayyah would rule. al-Qasim said: So we counted that, and it was a thousand, neither more nor less."
"2753","Ata b. Abi Rabah from al-Hasan b. Ali: al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad b. Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated to us, from Sa'id b. al-Marzuban Abu Sa'd, from Ata, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked. A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, how will some of us see others? He said: Eyes that day will be staring. So he raised his sight to heaven, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to cover my nakedness. He said: O Allah, cover her nakedness."
"2754","Ishaq b. Buzruj from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Muttalib b. Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me: Ishaq b. Buzruj narrated to me, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to wear the best we find, to perfume ourselves with the best we find, to sacrifice the fattest we find - a cow for seven, and a camel for ten - and to manifest takbir, with tranquility and dignity upon us."
"2755","Suwayd b. Ghafalah from al-Hasan b. Ali: Ali b. Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Humayd al-Razi narrated to us: Salamah b. al-Fadl narrated to us: Amr b. Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ibrahim b. Abd al-A'la, from Suwayd b. Ghafalah, who said: A'ishah bint Khalifah al-Khath'amiyyah was with al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. When Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was struck and allegiance was given to al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, for the caliphate, he entered upon her and she said: May the caliphate please you. He said to her: Do you show gloating at the killing of Ali? Go, you are divorced thrice. So she covered herself with a cloak of hers and sat in a corner of the house, saying: By Allah, I did not intend what you took it for. She remained until her waiting period ended, then moved away from him; so he sent to her the remainder remaining for her of her dowry upon him, and a provision of ten thousand. When the messenger came to her with that, she said: A small provision from a parting beloved. When the messenger returned to al-Hasan and informed him of what she said, al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, wept and said: Were it not that I heard my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or: I heard my father narrating from my grandfather that he said: When a man divorces his wife thrice at the menstrual periods, or divorces her thrice ambiguously, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband - I would have taken her back."
"2756","Ali b. Abi Talhah from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Ali b. Ishaq al-Wazir al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ismail b. Musa al-Sadusi narrated to us: Said b. Khaytham al-Hilali narrated to us: from al-Walid b. Yasar al-Hamdani, from Ali b. Abi Talhah, freedman of Banu Umayyah, who said: Muawiyah b. Abi Sufyan performed Hajj, and Muawiyah b. Hudayj performed Hajj with him, and he was among the most foul-mouthed of people against Ali. He passed through Madinah in the mosque of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while al-Hasan b. Ali was sitting among a group of his companions. It was said to him: This is Muawiyah b. Hudayj, the one who reviles Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: Bring the man to me. The messenger came to him and said: Answer. He said: Who? He said: Al-Hasan b. Ali is calling you. So he came to him and greeted him. Al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Are you Muawiyah b. Hudayj? He said: Yes. He repeated it to him three times. Al-Hasan said to him: The one who reviles Ali? It was as if he felt ashamed. Al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Nay, by Allah, if you come to him at the Hawd, and I do not think you will come to it, you will find him with his lower garment rolled up on his leg, driving away the hypocrites as stray camels are driven away; the statement of the truthful one believed (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {And he has failed who invents falsehood}."
"2757","Fulfalah al-Jufi from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Muhammad b. Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Said al-Jawhari narrated to us: Said b. Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us: Fudayl b. Ghazwan narrated to us: Abu al-Mughirah al-Dhuhli narrated to us: Fulfalah al-Jufi narrated to me, who said: I heard al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream clinging to the Throne, and I saw Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, holding the waist of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, holding the waist of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and I saw Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, holding the waist of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and I saw blood pouring down from the sky to the earth. Al-Hasan narrated this hadith while some Shiites were with him, and they said: And what did you see of Ali? Al-Hasan said: There was no one I would have loved more to see holding the waist of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than Ali, but it was a dream I saw."
"2758","Al-Asbagh b. Nubatah from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Ibrahim b. Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us: Ismail b. Sayf narrated to us: Jafar b. Sulayman narrated to us: from Sad b. Tarif, from al-Asbagh b. Nubatah, who said: I entered with Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, to visit al-Hasan b. Ali when he was ill. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: How are you this morning, O son of the Messenger of Allah? He said: I am, praise be to Allah, recovered. He said: Likewise, if Allah wills. Then al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Prop me up. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, propped him against his chest, and he said: I heard my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: In Paradise there is a tree called the tree of tribulation; the people of affliction will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and no register will be raised for them, nor will a scale be set up for them; reward will be poured upon them in abundance. And he recited: {Only those who are patient shall receive their reward without account}."
"2759","Abu Jamilah from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: Mahmud b. Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Wahb b. Baqiyyah narrated to us: Khalid informed us: from Husayn, from Abu Jamilah: that al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, was appointed successor. While he was leading the people in prayer, a man leapt upon him and stabbed him with a dagger in his hip, and he remained ill from it for months. Then he stood on the minbar delivering a sermon and said: O people of Iraq, fear Allah concerning us, for we are your rulers and your guests, and we are the People of the House about whom Allah, mighty and majestic, said: {Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly}. He kept speaking that day until no one was seen in the mosque except weeping."
"2760","Talhah b. Ubaydullah from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Ahmad b. Hammuyah Abu Sayyar al-Tustari narrated to us: Bishr b. Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us: Yahya b. Said al-Wasiti narrated to us: Yahya b. al-Ala narrated to us: from Talhah b. Ubaydullah, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever receives a gift while people are sitting with him, they are his partners in it."
"2761","Al-Qasim b. Muhammad al-Dallal narrated to us: Mukhawwal b. Ibrahim narrated to us: Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Sulayman, from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed food, and speak good words."
"2762","Umar b. Ishaq from al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: from Ibn Awn, from Umayr b. Ishaq: that Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, met al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, and said: Lift your garment so I may kiss where I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss. So he uncovered his belly, and he placed his hand upon his navel."
"2763","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Ibn Awn, from Umayr b. Ishaq: that Abu Hurayrah met al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, and he mentioned something similar."
"2764","236 - Al-Husayn b. Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, known as Abu Abdullah; mention of his birth, his description and his appearance, may Allah be pleased with him, and may Allah ennoble his face, and his father and mother. Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. Said al-Kindi narrated to us: Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated to us: from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father, who said: There was nothing between al-Hasan and al-Husayn except one menstrual cycle."
"2765","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Dirar b. Surad narrated to us: Abd al-Karim b. Yafur al-Jufi narrated to us: from Jabir, from Abu al-Shatha, from Bishr b. Ghalib, who said: I was with Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he saw al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, and said: O Abu Abdullah, I saw you upon the hands of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with his hands stained with blood, when you were brought when you were born; he cut your cord and wrapped you in a cloth, and he spat into your mouth and spoke words I do not know what they were. Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, had preceded him in cutting the navel cord of al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Do not precede me with it."
"2766","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. Salim narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Yusuf narrated to us: from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whoever is pleased to look at the most resembling of people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his neck to his face, let him look at al-Hasan b. Ali; and whoever is pleased to look at the most resembling of people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his neck to his ankle in build and complexion, let him look at al-Husayn b. Ali."
"2767","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: I found in the book of Uqbah b. Qabisah: My father narrated to us: from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from Ali, who said: Whoever wishes to look at the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his head to his neck, let him look at al-Hasan; and whoever wishes to look at what is from his neck downward, let him look at al-Husayn; they divided him between them."
"2768","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Awn b. Sallam narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Al-Hasan was the most resembling of people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the throat upward. And he mentioned something similar."
"2769","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abbad b. Abi Zaidah narrated to us: Yahya b. Zakariyya b. Abi Zaidah narrated to us: from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The most resembling of people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between his head and his throat is al-Hasan."
"2770","Ahmad b. Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us: Ahmad b. Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from Ali, who said: Al-Hasan is the most resembling of people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between the head and the throat."
"2771","Uthman b. Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Raja narrated to us: Israil informed us: from Abu Ishaq, from Hani b. Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When al-Hasan was born I named him Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? I said: Harb. He said: Rather, he is Hasan. When al-Husayn was born we named him Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Bring me my son; what did you name him? I said: Harb. He said: Rather, he is Husayn. When the third was born I named him Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? I said: Harb. He said: Rather, he is Muhassin. Then he said: I named them after the sons of Harun: Shabbar, Shabir and Mushabbir."
"2772","Muhammad b. Yahya b. Sahl b. Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us: Sahl b. Uthman narrated to us: Yahya b. Zakariyya b. Abi Zaidah narrated to us: from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani b. Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When al-Hasan b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was born, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? I said: I named him Harb. He said: Rather, he is Hasan. When al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was born, he came and said the like of his statement. I said: I named him Harb. He said: Rather, he is Husayn. When I gave birth to the third he came and said the like of his statement. I said: I named him Harb. He said: Rather, he is Muhassin. Then he said: I named them after the sons of Harun: Shabbar, Shabir and Mushabbir."
"2773","Muhammad b. Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ismail b. Amr al-Bajali narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from Hani b. Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I loved to take the kunyah Abu Harb. When al-Hasan was born I named him Harb, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: What did you name them? I said: I named him Harb. He said: He is al-Hasan."
"2774","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Yusuf narrated to us: from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani b. Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When al-Hasan was born I named him Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What did you name him? I said: Harb. He said: No, but name him Hasan. Then al-Husayn was born and I named him Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What did you name him? I said: Harb. He said: Rather, name him Husayn. Then another was born and I named him Harb. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you name him? I said: Harb. He said: Name him Muhsin."
"2775","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. Umar b. Aban narrated to us: Yahya b. Isa al-Ramli al-Tamimi narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us: from Salim b. Abi al-Jad, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I was a man who loved war. When al-Hasan was born I intended to name him Harb, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him al-Hasan. When al-Husayn was born I intended to name him Harb, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him al-Husayn. And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I named these two sons of mine after the two sons of Harun: Shabbar and Shabir."
"2776","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik b. Ismail narrated to us: Amr b. Hurayth narrated to us: Barzaah b. Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: from Abi al-Khalil, from Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I named them - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn - after the two sons of Harun: Shabar and Shubayr."
"2777","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya narrated to me: Husayn b. Muhammad narrated to us: Jarir b. Hazim narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Anas: that al-Husayn b. Ali used to dye with wasmah."
"2778","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ismail b. Abdullah b. Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us: Ubaydullah b. Amr narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Aqil, from Muhammad b. Ali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that he named his eldest son Hamzah, and he named Husayn Jafar after his uncle; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named them Hasan and Husayn."
"2779","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah and Abdullah b. Umar b. Aban narrated to us; they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar b. Hurayth, who said: I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, dyeing with henna and katam."
"2780","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Abd al-Aziz b. Rufay, from Qays, freedman of Khabbab, who said: I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, dyeing black."
"2781","Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali was killed on the day of Ashura in the year sixty-one, at the age of fifty-eight, and he used to dye with henna and katam."
"2782","Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father, who said: Ali was killed at the age of fifty-eight, and at that age al-Husayn b. Ali was killed, and at that age Ali b. al-Husayn died, and at that age Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Husayn died."
"2783","Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us: Husayn b. Ali al-Jufi narrated to us: from Sufyan b. Uyaynah, who said: I heard al-Mahdi ask Jafar: How old was Ali when he was killed? He said: Fifty-eight; and at that age al-Husayn b. Ali was killed."
"2784","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Jawwas al-Hanafi narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar b. Hurayth, who said: I saw al-Husayn b. Ali dyeing black."
"2785","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Kamil b. Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: from Abd al-Rahman b. Buzruj, who said: I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, the two sons of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, dyeing black, and al-Husayn used to leave the tuft on the lower lip."
"2786","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Asad narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Ibrahim b. Muhajir and Firas, from al-Shabi, who said: I visited al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he had dyed black."
"2787","Al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Muawiyah b. Hisham narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Ismail, from Jafar, from his father: that al-Husayn b. Ali used to dye black."
"2788","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Tahir b. Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Man b. Isa narrated to us: Abu Mashar informed me: from Said al-Maqburi, who said: I saw al-Husayn b. Ali dyeing black."
"2789","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. Umar b. Aban narrated to us: Sulaym b. Muslim informed us: from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ali b. al-Husayn: that al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to dye black."
"2790","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. Umar b. Aban narrated to us: Sulaym b. Muslim narrated to us: from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar b. Ata b. Abi al-Khuwar and Ubaydullah b. Abi Yazid; they said: We saw al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, dyeing with wasmah."
"2791","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us: Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, who said: The tailor who cut a shirt for al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me; he said: I said: Shall I make it at the top of the foot? He said: No. I said: Shall I make it below the ankles? He said: What is below the ankles is in the Fire."
"2792","Ibrahim b. Muhammad al-Hilali narrated to us: Ismail b. Amr al-Bajali narrated to us: Mustaqim b. Abd al-Malik narrated to us, who said: I saw upon al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, socks of raised khazz, and I saw them riding commercial mules."
"2793","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Jawwas narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar b. Hurayth, who said: I saw upon al-Husayn b. Ali a red cloak of khazz."
"2794","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani and al-Husayn b. Yazid al-Tahhan narrated to us; they said: al-Muttalib b. Ziyad narrated to us: from al-Suddi, who said: I saw al-Husayn b. Ali wearing a turban of khazz with his hair coming out from under the turban."
"2795","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Asad narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Ibrahim b. Muhajir and Firas, from al-Shabi, who said: I visited al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, while he was wearing a garment of khazz."
"2796","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Tahir b. Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Man b. Isa narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us: from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father: that al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to wear his ring on the left hand."
"2797","Al-Abbas b. al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Amr b. Awn narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq al-Kufi, from Abu Ukkashah al-Hamdani, who said: I saw upon al-Husayn on the day he was killed a cloak of sundus brocade."
"2798","Abu Hanifah Muhammad b. Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Yazid b. Amr b. al-Bara al-Ghanawi narrated to us: Sulayman b. al-Haytham narrated to us, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was circumambulating the House, and he wanted to touch the Stone, so the people made room for him, while al-Farazdaq b. Ghalib was looking at him. A man said: O Abu Firas, who is this? Al-Farazdaq said: ... his nose."
"2799","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya b. Hammad narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, from Abi Idris: al-Musayyab b. Najabah narrated to us, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Shall I not tell you about myself in particular and my household? We said: Yes indeed. He said: As for Hasan, he is a man of the bowl and the table, a youth among youths; if the two rings of the girth were to meet, he would not avail you in war even a sparrow's snare. As for Abdullah b. Jafar, he is a man of amusement, shade and falsehood. Let not the two sons of Abbas deceive you. As for me and Husayn, then I and Husayn: we are from you and you are from us. By Allah, I have feared lest these people gain the upper hand over you through their righteousness in their land and your corruption in your land, through their fulfillment of trust and your treachery, through their obedience to their leader and your disobedience to yours, through their unity upon their falsehood and your disunity upon your truth, until their reign lasts long, until they deem lawful every sacred thing of Allah, until neither settled land nor desert remains but their injustice enters it, until one of you becomes a follower of them, until the support of one of you from them becomes like the support of a slave from his master: when he is present he obeys him, and when he is absent from him he reviles him, until the richest among you therein becomes the one with the best opinion of Allah. If Allah grants you well-being, then accept it; and if you are tried, then be patient, for the good end belongs to the God-fearing."
"2800","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Husayn b. Ishaq narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us: from Fitr b. Khalifah, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Abi Idris, from al-Musayyab b. Najabah al-Fazari, who said: We were sitting with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and they mentioned his household. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: As for al-Hasan, he will not avail you in war even a sparrow's snare; as for Abdullah b. Jafar, he is a man of shade and the table; as for Husayn, he is from you and you are from him."
"2801","Abu al-Zinba Ruh b. al-Faraj narrated to us: Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth b. Sad narrated to me, who said: Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, died in Rajab with four nights elapsed thereof, and Yazid was appointed successor for two years. In the year sixty-one al-Husayn b. Ali and his companions, may Allah be pleased with them, were killed, ten nights elapsed of Muharram, on the day of Ashura. And al-Abbas b. Ali b. Abi Talib was killed, his mother Umm al-Banin of Amir; and Jafar b. Ali b. Abi Talib; and Abdullah b. Ali b. Abi Talib; and Uthman b. Ali b. Abi Talib; and Abu Bakr b. Ali b. Abi Talib, his mother Layla bt. Masud of Nahshal; and Ali b. al-Husayn b. Ali b. Abi Talib the elder, his mother Layla of Thaqif; and Abdullah b. al-Husayn, his mother al-Rabab bt. Imri al-Qays of Kalb; and Abu Bakr b. al-Husayn of an umm walad; and al-Qasim b. al-Hasan of an umm walad; and Awn b. Abdullah b. Jafar b. Abi Talib; and Jafar b. Aqil b. Abi Talib; and Muslim b. Aqil b. Abi Talib; and Sulayman, freedman of al-Husayn; and Abdullah, foster-child of al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them. And al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed at the age of fifty-eight."
"2802","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya b. Hassan narrated to us: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us: from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed at the age of fifty-eight."
"2803","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Salam b. Asim al-Razi narrated to us: Yahya b. Durays narrated to us: from Fitr, from Mundhir al-Thawri, who said: Whenever the killing of al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was mentioned in the presence of Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: Along with him were killed seventeen of those who had stirred in the womb of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2804","Abu al-Zinba Ruh b. al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us: Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, refused to be taken captive, so they fought him and killed him, and they killed his two sons and his companions who fought with him at a place called al-Taff. Ali b. Husayn, Fatimah bt. Husayn and Sukaynah bt. Husayn were taken to Ubaydullah b. Ziyad, Ali being on that day a youth who had reached puberty. He sent them to Yazid b. Muawiyah, who ordered Sukaynah to be placed behind his couch lest she see the head of her father and her relatives. Ali b. al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, was in fetters, and he put down his head and struck the front teeth of al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: ... Then Ali b. al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, said: {No calamity befalls on the earth or in yourselves except that it is in a Book before We bring it into being; indeed that is easy for Allah}. Yazid found it grievous to quote a verse of poetry, while Ali recited a verse from the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic. Yazid said: Rather, it is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had seen us shackled, he would have loved to free us from the fetters. He said: You have spoken the truth, so free them from the fetters. He said: And if we were to stand before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a distance, he would have loved to bring us near. He said: You have spoken the truth, so bring them near. Fatimah and Sukaynah began craning to see the head of their father, and Yazid began craning in his sitting place to screen the head of their father from them. Then he ordered them to be prepared, treated them kindly, and they were sent out to Madinah."
"2805","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us: Ismail b. Aban narrated to us: Hibban b. Ali narrated to us: from Sad b. Tarif, from Abu Jafar Muhammad b. Ali, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, will be killed sixty years after my emigration."
"2806","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us: Ismail b. Aban narrated to us: Hibban b. Ali narrated to me: from Sad b. Tarif, from Abu Jafar, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Husayn will be killed when grayness covers him. Abu al-Qasim said: Al-qatir means gray hair."
"2807","Al-Qasim b. Abbad al-Khattabi al-Basri narrated to us: Said b. Subayh narrated to us, who said: Hisham b. al-Kalbi said: from Awanah b. al-Hakam, who said: When Abd al-Rahman b. Muljam struck Ali, may Allah be pleased with him... and he mentioned the hadith."
"2808","Ishaq b. Ibrahim narrated to us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father: that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed at the age of fifty-eight; and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed at the age of fifty-eight; and Ali b. al-Husayn died at the age of fifty-eight."
"2809","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ubayd narrated to us: Shurahbil b. Mudrik al-Jufi narrated to me: from Abdullah b. Nujayy, from his father: that he travelled with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and when he came parallel to Nineveh he said: Patience, O Abu Abdullah, patience on the bank of the Euphrates. I said: What is that? He said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while his eyes were overflowing, and I said: Has anyone angered you, O Messenger of Allah? Why do I see your eyes overflowing? He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, rose from my presence and informed me that my nation will kill al-Husayn, my son. Then he said: Would you like me to show you some of his soil? I said: Yes. He stretched out his hand and took a handful; when I saw it I could not hold back my eyes from overflowing."
"2810","Muhammad b. Ali al-Saigh narrated to us: Yaqub b. Humayd b. Kasib narrated to us: Sufyan b. Hamzah narrated to us: from Kathir b. Zayd, from al-Muttalib b. Abdullah b. Hantab, who said: When al-Husayn b. Ali was surrounded, he said: What is the name of this land? It was said: Karbala. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth: it is a land of grief and tribulation."
"2811","Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: Abd al-Samad b. Hassan al-Marwazi narrated to us. And Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami, Muhammad b. Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri and Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us; they said: Shayban b. Farrukh narrated to us; they said: Umarah b. Zadahan al-Saydalani narrated to us; they said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us: from Anas b. Malik, who said: The angel of rain sought permission from his Lord, mighty and majestic, to visit the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and He permitted him. He came to him while he was in the house of Umm Salamah, and he said: O Umm Salamah, guard the door for us; let no one enter upon us. While they were at the door, al-Husayn came and opened the door, and began leaping upon the back of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced and kissed him. The angel said to him: Do you love him, O Muhammad? He said: Yes. He said: Yet your nation will kill him; and if you wish, I can show you some of the soil of the place where he will be killed. He said: He took a handful from the place where he will be killed and brought him a reddish soft soil. Umm Salamah took it and placed it in her garment. Thabit said: We used to say it is Karbala."
"2812","Ahmad b. Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us: Amr b. Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: from Abi al-Aswad, from Urwah b. al-Zubayr, from Aishah, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with her, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while revelation was coming to him. He climbed upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was bent over, and played upon his back. Jibril said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you love him, O Muhammad? He said: O Jibril, why would I not love my son? He said: Yet your nation will kill him after you. Jibril, peace be upon him, stretched out his hand and brought him a white soil, saying: In this land this son of yours will be killed, O Muhammad, and its name is al-Taff. When Jibril, peace be upon him, left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with the soil in his hand, weeping, and said: O Aishah, Jibril, peace be upon him, informed me that al-Husayn, my son, will be killed in the land of al-Taff, and that my nation will be put to trial after me. Then he went out to his companions, among them Ali, Abu Bakr, Umar, Hudhayfah, Ammar and Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with them, while he was weeping. They said: What makes you weep, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Jibril informed me that my son al-Husayn will be killed after me in the land of al-Taff; he brought me this soil and informed me that therein is his resting place."
"2813","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Husayn b. Hurayth narrated to us: al-Fadl b. Musa narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Said, from his father, from Aishah: that al-Husayn b. Ali entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, shall I not amaze you? An angel who had never entered upon me before has just entered upon me, saying: This son of mine will be killed. He said: If you wish, I will show you a soil where he will be killed. The angel took with his hand and showed me a red soil."
"2814","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Hudbah narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us: from Ali b. Zayd, from Ali b. al-Husayn, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali said to me a day before his killing: The Children of Israil had a king... and he mentioned the hadith."
"2815","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Abbad b. Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to me: Amr b. Thabit narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Abu Wail Shaqiq b. Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: Al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, were playing before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in my house, when Jibril, peace be upon him, descended and said: O Muhammad, your nation will kill this son of yours after you. He gestured with his hand toward al-Husayn. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept and pressed him to his chest. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This soil is a trust with you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smelled it and said: Alas, grief and tribulation. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Salamah, when this soil turns to blood, then know that my son has been killed. He said: Umm Salamah placed it in a bottle, then she would look at it every day, saying: A day on which you turn to blood is indeed a grave day."
"2816","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; they said: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us. And Abu Khalifah al-Fadl b. al-Hubab narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; they said: Abd al-Hamid b. Bahram narrated to us: from Shahr b. Hawshab, who said: I heard Umm Salamah, when the news of the death of al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came, curse the people of Iraq, saying: They killed him, may Allah, mighty and majestic, kill them; they deceived him and humiliated him, may Allah curse them."
"2817","Al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us: from Kathir b. Zayd, from Abd al-Muttalib b. Abdullah b. Hantab, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting one day in my house and said: Let no one enter upon me. I waited, then al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, entered. I heard the sobbing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping. I looked in, and Husayn was in his lap, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wiping his forehead and weeping. I said: By Allah, I did not know when he entered. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, was with us in the house, and he said: Do you love him? I said: As for this world, yes. He said: Your nation will kill him in a land called Karbala. Jibril, peace be upon him, took some of its soil and showed it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When Husayn was surrounded at his killing, he said: What is the name of this land? They said: Karbala. He said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth; a land of grief and tribulation."
"2818","Al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ali b. Bahr narrated to us: Isa b. Yunus narrated to us. And Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yala b. Ubayd narrated to us; they said: Musa b. Salih al-Juhani narrated to us: from Salih b. Arbad, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Sit at the door, and let no one come in to me. I stood at the door, when al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, came. I went to take hold of him, but the boy beat me to it and entered upon his grandfather. I said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, you ordered me that no one should come in to you, yet your son came; I went to take hold of him but he beat me to it. When that lasted long I looked in from the door and found you turning something over with your hands while your tears flowed, with the boy upon your belly. He said: Yes, Jibril came to me and informed me that my nation will kill him, and brought me the soil upon which he will be killed; it is what I am turning over with my hands."
"2819","Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us: Jafar b. Musafir al-Tinnisi narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Musa b. Yaqub al-Zami narrated to us: from Hashim b. Hashim b. Utbah b. Abi Waqqas, from Utbah b. Abdullah b. Zamaah, from Umm Salamah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lay down one day, then awoke heavy in spirit, with a red soil in his hand which he was turning over. I said: What is this soil, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, informed me that this one - meaning al-Husayn - will be killed in the land of Iraq. I said to Jibril, peace be upon him: Show me the soil of the land where he will be killed; this is its soil."
"2820","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Harb narrated to us; they said: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us: from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream at midday, disheveled and dusty, with a bottle in his hand containing blood. I said: May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: The blood of al-Husayn and his companions; I have been gathering it since today. That day was recorded, and it was found that he had been killed on that very day."
"2821","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Sad b. Wahb al-Wasiti narrated to us: Jafar b. Sulayman narrated to us: from Shubayl b. Ghazarah, from Abi Hibarah, who said: I accompanied Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, until he came to Kufah. He ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: How will you be when the offspring of your Prophet descend among you? They said: Then we shall do our utmost for Allah concerning them. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, they will indeed descend among you, and you will indeed go out against them and kill them. Then he began saying: ..."
"2822","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. al-Hakam b. Abi Ziyad and Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us; they said: Ubaydullah b. Musa narrated to us: from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani b. Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Al-Husayn will indeed be killed, and I know the soil where he will be killed, near the two rivers."
"2823","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Sallam Abu Shurahbil, from Abi Harthamah, who said: I was with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, at the two rivers of Karbala. He passed by a tree under which were gazelle droppings; he took a handful of it and smelled it, then said: From this ridge seventy thousand will be mustered who will enter Paradise without account."
"2824","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Yahya b. Abi Saminah narrated to us: Yahya b. Hammad narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us: from Ata b. al-Saib, from Maymun b. Mihran, from Shayban b. Mukharrim, who was an Uthmani, who said: I was with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, when he came to Karbala and said: In this place martyrs will be killed the like of whom there are no martyrs except the martyrs of Badr. I said: Some of his lies; and there was the leg of a dead donkey. I said to my boy: Take the leg of this donkey, stake it in his sitting place and conceal it. Time struck its blow, and when al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, was killed, I set out with some companions of mine, and there was the corpse of al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, upon the leg of that donkey, with his companions fallen around him."
"2825","Muhammad b. Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us: Muhammad b. Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Kathir narrated to us: from Husayn b. Abd al-Rahman, from al-Ala b. Abi Aishah, from his father, from Ras al-Jalut, who said: We used to hear that a son of a prophet would be killed at Karbala. Whenever I entered it I would spur my horse until I passed beyond it. When al-Husayn was killed, thereafter I would travel through it in my usual manner."
"2826","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Furat b. Mahbub narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated to us: Aslam al-Minqari narrated to me, who said: I entered upon al-Hajjaj, then Sinan b. Anas, the killer of al-Husayn, entered - an aged dark man with henna in his beard, long-nosed, with vitiligo on his face. He was stood before al-Hajjaj, and al-Hajjaj looked at him and said: Did you kill al-Husayn? He said: Yes. He said: And how did you do it with him? He said: I propped him with the spear and hacked him with the sword. Al-Hajjaj said to him: You two shall never be together in one abode."
"2827","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Said b. Khuthaym narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Khalid al-Dabbi, from Ibrahim, who said: Had I been among those who killed al-Husayn b. Ali, then been forgiven, then admitted to Paradise, I would be ashamed to pass by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he looks at my face."
"2828","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Bakr b. Khalaf narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us. And Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Said al-Jawhari narrated to us: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us; both from Qurrah b. Khalid, who said: I heard Abu Raja al-Utaridi say: Do not revile Ali nor the people of this House, for a neighbor of ours from Balhujaym said: Have you not seen this sinner al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah kill him - so Allah struck him with two stars in his eyes, and Allah blinded him."
"2829","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us: Abu Ghassan informed us: Abd al-Salam b. Harb narrated to us: from Abd al-Malik b. Kurdus, from the chamberlain of Ubaydullah b. Ziyad, who said: I entered the palace behind Ubaydullah b. Ziyad when al-Husayn was killed, and fire blazed in his face. He did like this with his sleeve over his face and said: Did you see? I said: Yes. Then he ordered me to conceal that."
"2830","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: from al-Amash, from Umarah b. Umayr, who said: When the head of Ubaydullah b. Ziyad and his companions was brought, it was set up in the open courtyard. I came to them while they were saying: It has come, it has come - and there was a snake that came threading through the heads until it entered the nostril of Ubaydullah. It remained a while, then came out and went away. Then they said: It has come - and it did that two or three times."
"2831","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Salm b. Junadah narrated to us: Ahmad b. Bashir narrated to us: from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, who said: I saw in a dream as if men descended from the sky with spears, pursuing the killers of al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him. It was not long before al-Mukhtar came down and killed them."
"2832","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yazid b. Mihran Abu Khalid narrated to us: Asbat b. Muhammad narrated to us: from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from al-Zuhri, who said: When al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, no stone in Bayt al-Maqdis was lifted but fresh blood was found beneath it."
"2833","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: al-Dahhak b. Makhlad narrated to us: from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, who said: No stone in Syria was lifted on the day al-Husayn b. Ali was killed but from blood, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2834","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Minjab b. al-Harith narrated to us: Ali b. Mushir narrated to us: My grandmother Umm Hakim narrated to me, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali was killed when I was a young girl; the sky remained for days like a blood clot."
"2835","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. Yahya b. al-Rabi b. Abi Rashid al-Kahili narrated to us: Mansur b. Abi Nuwayrah narrated to us: from Abu Bakr b. Ayyash, from Jamil b. Zayd, who said: When al-Husayn was killed the sky turned red. I said: What are you saying? He said: The liar is a hypocrite; the sky turned red when he was killed."
"2836","Qays b. Abi Qays al-Bukhari narrated to us: Qutaybah b. Said narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: from Abu Qabil, who said: When al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, the sun eclipsed so that the stars appeared at midday, until we thought it was night."
"2837","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: My father narrated to me: from my grandfather, from Isa b. al-Harith al-Kindi, who said: When al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, we remained seven days: when we prayed Asr we would look at the sun upon the edges of the walls as if it were saffron-dyed sheets, and we would look at the stars striking one another."
"2838","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us: from Hisham b. Hassan, from Muhammad b. Sirin, who said: There was no redness in the sky until al-Husayn was killed."
"2839","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us: Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Abd al-Salam b. Harb narrated to us: from al-Kalbi, who said: A man shot al-Husayn while he was drinking, and his jaw was paralyzed. He said: May Allah never quench your thirst. He said: He drank until he burst."
"2840","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Zubayr b. Bakkar narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Hasan narrated to us, who said: When Umar b. Sad encamped against Husayn, and he was certain they would kill him, he stood among his companions as a speaker. He praised Allah, mighty and majestic, and extolled Him, then said: What you see of the affair has come to pass; this world has changed and become unrecognizable, its good has turned away and continued until nothing remains of it except like the dregs of a vessel, save a mean livelihood like foul pasture. Do you not see that truth is not acted upon and falsehood is not restrained? Let the believer desire meeting Allah. I see death only as happiness, and life with the wrongdoers only as disgust. Al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed on the day of Ashura in the year sixty-one at al-Taff in Karbala, wearing a dark khazz cloak, dyed black, at the age of fifty-six."
"2841","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Zubayr narrated to us: Ahmad b. Salman narrated to me: from Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi, from Jafar b. Muhammad, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the pledge from al-Hasan, al-Husayn, Abdullah b. Abbas and Abdullah b. Jafar, may Allah be pleased with them, while they were small and had not reached maturity. He said: And he took the pledge from no small child except from us."
"2842","Ali narrated to us: al-Zubayr narrated to us, who said: My uncle Musab b. Abdullah narrated to me, who said: Al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, performed twenty-five pilgrimages on foot."
"2843","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Zubayr b. Bakkar narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Dahhak b. Uthman al-Hizami narrated to me, who said: The body of al-Husayn resembled the body of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2844","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Zubayr b. Bakkar narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Dahhak b. Uthman al-Hizami narrated to me: from his father, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, set out to Kufah in anger at the rule of Yazid b. Muawiyah. Yazid b. Muawiyah wrote to Ubaydullah b. Ziyad, his governor over Iraq: It has reached me that Husayn has marched to Kufah; your time has been afflicted with him apart from all times, your land apart from all lands, and you have been afflicted with him apart from all officials; at this point one is either freed or returns a slave as slaves are enslaved. So Ubaydullah b. Ziyad killed him and sent his head to him. When it was placed before him he quoted the verse of al-Husayn b. al-Humam: ..."
"2845","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Abd al-Salam b. Harb narrated to us: from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the house of Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and passed by the house of Fatimah. He heard Husayn weeping, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Do you not know that his weeping hurts me?"
"2846","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Zubayr narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Hasan al-Makhzumi narrated to me, who said: When the household of al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought before Yazid b. Muawiyah, and his head was placed before him, Yazid wept and said: ... By Allah, had I been his companion I would never have killed him. Ali b. al-Husayn said: Not so. He said: How, O son of my mother? He said: {No calamity befalls on the earth or in yourselves except that it is in a Book before We bring it into being; indeed that is easy for Allah}. Abd al-Rahman Ibn Umm al-Hakam was with him, and Abd al-Rahman said: ... Then Yazid raised his hand, struck the chest of Abd al-Rahman and said: Be silent."
"2847","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad b. Said b. al-Asbahani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Ata b. al-Saib, from Ibn Wail or Wail b. Alqamah, who witnessed what happened there, who said: A man stood and said: Is Husayn among you? They said: Yes. He said: Glad tidings of the Fire. He said: Glad tidings of a Merciful Lord and an obeyed intercessor. He said: Who are you? He said: I am Ibn Juwayzah - or Huwayzah. He said: O Allah, drag him to the Fire. His mount bolted with him, and his foot caught in the stirrup. He said: By Allah, nothing remained of him upon it except his foot."
"2848","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said when he sensed death: Bring me a garment no one will desire, to place under my clothes so I am not stripped. It was said to him: Drawers? He said: No; that is the dress of one upon whom humiliation has been imposed. So he took a garment, tore it, and placed it under his clothes. When he was killed they stripped him."
"2849","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Abd al-Jabbar b. al-Abbas narrated to us: from Ammar al-Duhni, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by Kab and said: A man from the offspring of this man will be killed among a band; the sweat of their horses will not dry before they come to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, passed, and they said: Is this he, O Abu Ishaq? He said: No. Husayn passed, and they said: Is this he? He said: Yes."
"2850","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Zubayr b. Bakkar narrated to us, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was born five nights elapsed of Shaban in the year four of the Hijrah, and was killed on Friday, the day of Ashura in Muharram in the year sixty-one. Sinan b. Abi Anas al-Nakhai killed him, Khawli b. Yazid al-Asbahi of Himyar finished him off, severed his head and brought it to Ubaydullah b. Ziyad. Sinan b. Anas said: Fill ..."
"2851","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Zubayr narrated to us: from his uncle Musab b. Abdullah, who said: Zaynab the younger, daughter of Aqil b. Abi Talib, went out to the people at al-Baqi weeping for her slain at al-Taff, saying: ... Abu al-Aswad al-Duali said: We say: {Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves} - the verse; then Abu al-Aswad al-Duali said: ..."
"2852","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us: from Abu Musa, from al-Hasan, who said: Along with al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, sixteen men of his household were killed; by Allah, on that day there was no household on the face of the earth resembling them. Sufyan said: And who can doubt this?"
"2853","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Fitr b. Khalifah narrated to us: from Mundhir al-Thawri, who said: Whenever we mentioned Husayn and those killed with him, may Allah be pleased with them, Muhammad b. al-Hanafiyyah would say: Along with him were killed seventeen youths, all of whom had stirred in the womb of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her."
"2854","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Abdullah al-Harawi narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Abu Mashar narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Said b. al-As, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abd al-Malik b. Marwan said to me: Which one are you if you inform me what sign there was on the day al-Husayn b. Ali was killed? I said: No pebble in Bayt al-Maqdis was lifted but fresh blood was found beneath it. Abd al-Malik said: You and I are partners in this hadith."
"2855","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ismail narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: My grandmother, the mother of my father, narrated to me, who said: Two men of the Jufis witnessed the killing of al-Husayn b. Ali. She said: As for one of them, his member grew long until he would wrap it; as for the other, he would face the waterskin with his mouth until he finished it. Sufyan said: I saw the child of one of them as if afflicted, as if mad."
"2856","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ismail narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: My grandmother, the mother of my father, narrated to me, who said: I saw the wars dye taken from the camp of al-Husayn turn to ashes."
"2857","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ishaq narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Ibrahim b. Maysarah, from Tawus, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Husayn sought my permission to go out, and I said: Were it not that it would disgrace me or you, I would clasp my hand in your head. He said: What he answered me was to say: To be killed in such-and-such place is dearer to me than that the sanctuary of Allah and His Messenger be violated through me. He said: That is what consoled me concerning him."
"2858","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Marwazi narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us: from al-Amash, who said: A man of Banu Asad defecated upon the grave of Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: Madness, insanity, leprosy, illness and poverty befell the people of that house."
"2859","Al-Hasan b. al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us: Sulaym b. Mansur b. Ammar narrated to us: My father narrated to us. And Ahmad b. Yahya b. Khalid b. Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us: Amr b. Bukayr b. Bakkar al-Qanabi narrated to us: Mujashi b. Amr narrated to us; they said: Abdullah b. Lahiah narrated to us: from Abu Qabil: Abdullah b. Amr b. al-As narrated to me that Muadh b. Jabal informed him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us changed in color, and said: I am Muhammad; I have been given the beginnings of speech and its endings. Obey me as long as I am among you; when I am taken away, then hold to the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic: deem lawful its lawful and deem unlawful its unlawful. There has come to you comfort and rest, a Book from Allah foreordained. There will come to you trials like pieces of the dark night; whenever some messengers go, messengers come. Prophethood has been succeeded and become kingship. May Allah have mercy upon whoever takes it by its right and leaves it as he entered it. Hold, O Muadh, and count. He said: When I reached five he said: Yazid - may Allah not bless Yazid. Then his eyes (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears. Then he said: Husayn has been announced to me as dead; I have been given his soil and informed of his killer. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he will not be killed among a people who do not defend him but Allah will set their hearts and minds at variance, empower their wicked over them, and clothe them in factions. Then he said: Alas for the chicks of the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from an appointed luxurious successor who will kill my successor and the successor of the successor. Hold, O Muadh. When I reached ten he said: Al-Walid - the name of a Pharaoh, demolisher of the laws of Islam before him; a man of a household from whom Allah draws His sword with no sheath for it. The people differed and became like this - and he interlaced his fingers. Then he said: After one hundred and twenty, swift death and extensive killing; therein is their destruction, and a man of the offspring of al-Abbas will rule over them."
"2860","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us: from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The jinn were heard lamenting over al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2861","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us: Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Abu Numayr, uncle of al-Hasan b. Shuayb, narrated to us: from Abu Humayd al-Tahhan, who said: I was among Khuzaah when something from the estate of al-Husayn was brought. It was said to them: Shall we slaughter or sell and divide? He said: Slaughter. He said: He sat upon a large bowl; when it was placed it burst into flame."
"2862","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Ismail b. Musa al-Suddi narrated to us: Dhuwayd al-Jufi narrated to us: from his father, who said: When al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, a camel from his camp was plundered; when it was cooked it turned to blood, so they overturned it."
"2863","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Surayj b. Yunus narrated to us: Umar b. Abd al-Rahman Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us: from Ismail b. Abd al-Rahman al-Azdi, from Abu Janab, who said: The jinn were heard weeping over al-Husayn b. Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2864","Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jandal b. Waliq narrated to us: Abdullah b. al-Tufayl narrated to us: from Abu Zayd al-Fuqaymi, from Abu Janab al-Kalbi: The plaster-makers narrated to me, saying: When we would go out at night to the cemetery at the place where al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, we would hear the jinn lamenting over him, saying: ..."
"2865","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Hudbah b. Khalid narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us: from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Umm Salamah, who said: The jinn were heard lamenting over al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2866","Abdullah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us: from Ammar, from Maymunah, who said: The jinn were heard lamenting over al-Husayn."
"2867","Al-Qasim b. Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us: Suwayd b. Said narrated to us: Amr b. Thabit narrated to us, who said: Umm Salamah said: I have not heard the lamentation of the jinn since the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away except tonight, and I do not think my son has been killed - meaning al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him. She said to her slave-girl: Go out and ask. She was informed that he had been killed, and a female jinn was lamenting: ... with effort."
"2868","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah b. al-Hakam b. Abi Ziyad narrated to us: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us: Yunus b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us: from Abu Ishaq, from Amr b. Bajalah, who said: The first humiliation to enter upon the Arabs was the killing of al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and the claiming of Ziyad as kin."
"2869","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us: Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Nuh b. Darraj narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Umar b. Ali b. Husayn, from his father, who said: Al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed while heavily in debt; Ali b. Husayn sold concerning it such-and-such spring and such-and-such spring."
"2870","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Musa b. Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Bishr narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Abi al-Jahhaf, from Musa b. Umayr, from his father, who said: Al-Husayn ordered a caller, who called out: Let no man burdened with debt come with us. A man said: My wife has guaranteed my debt. Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, said: And what is the guarantee of a woman?"
"2871","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman b. Salih al-Asadi narrated to us: al-Sari b. Mansur b. Ammar narrated to us: from his father, from Ibn Lahiah, from Abu Qabil, who said: When al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, was killed, they severed his head and sat at the first stage drinking nabidh, passing the head around in greeting. An iron pen came out to them from a wall and wrote in a line of blood: ... Then they fled and left the head; then they returned."
"2872","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ghurak narrated to us: Abu Said al-Taghlibi narrated to us: from Yahya b. Yaman, from an imam of Banu Sulaym, from elders of his who raided the Byzantines: they lodged in one of their churches and read upon a written stone: ... We asked them: How long ago was this church built? They said: Three hundred years before your Prophet was sent. Abu Jafar al-Hadrami said: And Jandal b. Waliq narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Ghurak; then I heard it from Muhammad b. Ghurak."
"2873","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, who said: I heard Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Humayd al-Jahmi, of the offspring of Abu Jahm b. Hudhayfah, reciting concerning the killing of al-Husayn, saying this poetry is by Zaynab bt. Aqil b. Abi Talib: ... Abu al-Aswad al-Duali said: We say: {We have wronged ourselves, and if You do not forgive us and have mercy upon us, we shall surely be among the losers}."
"2874","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Ahmad b. Humayd al-Jahmi narrated to us: al-Waqidi narrated to us: from Isa b. Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from al-Shabi, who said: The head of al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, was the first head carried in Islam."
"2875","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ubayd b. Ismail al-Habbari narrated to us: Said b. Suwayd narrated to us: from Abd al-Malik b. Umayr, who said: I entered upon Ubaydullah b. Ziyad while the head of al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was before him upon a shield. By Allah, I had remained only a little before I entered upon al-Mukhtar while the head of Ubaydullah b. Ziyad was upon a shield. By Allah, I had remained only a little before I entered upon Musab b. al-Zubayr while the head of al-Mukhtar was upon a shield. By Allah, I had remained only a little before I entered upon Abd al-Malik b. Marwan while the head of Musab b. al-Zubayr was upon a shield."
"2876","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Harb narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us: from Ali b. Zayd, from Anas b. Malik, who said: When the head of al-Husayn b. Ali was brought to Ubaydullah b. Ziyad, he began tapping with a rod in his hand, saying: He had beautiful front teeth. I said: By Allah, I shall surely grieve you; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing the place of your rod upon his mouth."
"2877","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Husayn b. Ubaydullah al-Kufi narrated to us: al-Nadr b. Shumayl narrated to us: Hisham b. Hassan narrated to us: from Hafsah bt. Sirin, from Anas, who said: I was with Ibn Ziyad when the head of al-Husayn was brought; he began saying with a rod at his nose: I have never seen such beauty. I said: Yet he was among those of them most resembling the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2878","Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us: from Abdullah b. Sharik, from Bishr b. Ghalib, from al-Husayn b. Ali, who said: Whoever loves us for this world - the possessor of this world is loved by the righteous and the wicked alike; and whoever loves us for Allah, we and he will be on the Day of Resurrection like these two. And he pointed with the index and middle fingers."
"2879","Yahya b. Uthman b. Salih, Muttalib b. Shuayb al-Azdi and Ahmad b. Rishdin the Egyptians narrated to us; they said: Ibrahim b. Hammad b. Abi Hazim al-Madani narrated to us: Imran b. Muhammad b. Said b. al-Musayyab narrated to us: from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has three sanctities; whoever preserves them, Allah preserves for him the affair of his religion and his world; and whoever does not preserve them, Allah preserves nothing for him: the sanctity of Islam, my sanctity, and the sanctity of my kin."
"2880","Abu al-Zinba Ruh b. al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us: Yusuf b. Adi narrated to us: Hammad b. al-Mukhtar narrated to us: from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Anas b. Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I have been given al-Kawthar. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Kawthar? He said: A river in Paradise, its width and length between the east and the west; none drinks from it and then thirsts, none performs ablution from it and then becomes disheveled. No man shall drink from it who violated my covenant or killed my household."
"2881","Ahmad b. Shuayb al-Nasai narrated to us: Qutaybah b. Said informed us: Ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us: from Ubaydullah b. Abd al-Rahman b. Mawhab, from Amrah, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Six I have cursed, and every prophet whose prayer is answered has cursed: the one who adds to the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic; the one who denies the decree of Allah; the one who deems lawful the sacred things of Allah; the one who deems lawful from my progeny what Allah has forbidden; and the one who abandons the Sunnah."
"2882","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; they said: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Mahdi b. Maymun narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Abi Yaqub, from Ibn Abi Num, who said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man asked him about the blood of a mosquito. He said: From where are you? He said: From the people of Iraq. He said: Look at this one - he asks me about the blood of a mosquito, yet they killed the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They are my two sweet basils in this world."
"2883","And what al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, transmitted with isnad: Ali b. al-Husayn from his father, may Allah be pleased with them. Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us: from Umarah b. Ghaziyyah, from Abdullah b. Ali b. al-Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The miser is he in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me."
"2884","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Musa b. Dawud narrated to us: Abdullah b. Umar narrated to us: from Ibn Shihab, from Ali b. Husayn, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the excellence of a man's Islam is his leaving what does not concern him."
"2885","Yusuf b. al-Hakam al-Dabbi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Bashir al-Kindi narrated to us: Ubaydah b. Humayd narrated to us: Fitr b. Khalifah narrated to me: from Abu Jafar Muhammad b. Ali b. Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather Husayn b. Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever I am mentioned in his presence and he misses invoking blessings upon me has missed the path to Paradise."
"2886","Muhammad b. al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Said b. Sulayman narrated to us: al-Hayyaj b. Bistam narrated to us: Anbasah narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Sulayman, from Ali b. al-Husayn, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten days of itikaf in Ramadan are like two Hajjes and two Umrahs."
"2887","Al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us: Ali b. Qadim narrated to us: from Abd al-Salam b. Harb, from Yahya b. Said, from Ali b. al-Husayn, from his father, who said: Love us with the love of Islam, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not raise me above my due, for Allah the Exalted took me as a servant before He took me as a Messenger."
"2888","Ishaq b. Muhammad al-Harraji al-Makki and al-Abbas b. Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us; they said: Abd al-Jabbar b. al-Ala narrated to us: Abdullah b. Maymun al-Qaddah narrated to us: Jafar b. Muhammad narrated to us: from his father, from Ali b. Husayn, who said: I heard my father say: Three days before the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Jibril, peace be upon him, descended upon him and said: O Muhammad, Allah, mighty and majestic, has sent me to you to honor you, to prefer you, and as a distinction for you. He asks you about what He knows better than you: He says: How do you find yourself? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I find myself, O Jibril, grieved, and I find myself, O Jibril, distressed. He said: When the third day came, Jibril, peace be upon him, descended, the Angel of Death, peace be upon them both, descended, and with them descended an angel in the air called Ismail, over seventy thousand angels, with no angel among them but over seventy thousand angels, escorted by Jibril, peace be upon him. He said: O Muhammad, Allah, mighty and majestic, has sent me to you to honor you, to prefer you, and as a distinction for you. He asks you about what He knows better than you: He says: How do you find yourself? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I find myself, O Jibril, grieved, and I find myself, O Jibril, distressed. He said: The Angel of Death sought permission at the door. Jibril, peace be upon him, said: O Muhammad, this is the Angel of Death seeking permission to enter upon you; he has never sought permission from any human before you, nor will he seek permission from any human after you. He said: Give him permission. Jibril, peace be upon him, gave him permission. He came forward until he stood before him and said: O Muhammad, Allah, mighty and majestic, has sent me to you and commanded me to obey you in whatever you command me: if you command me to take your soul I shall take it, and if you dislike it I shall leave it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Will you do so, O Angel of Death? He said: Yes, and with that I have been commanded: to obey you in whatever you command me. Jibril, peace be upon him, said to him: Allah, mighty and majestic, has longed to meet you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Proceed with what you have been commanded. Jibril said to him: This is my last treading upon the earth; my need was only in this world. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and the condolence came, a visitor came whose voice they heard but whose person they did not see, saying: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; every soul shall taste death. In Allah is consolation from every calamity, a successor from every perishing one, and recompense for all that is missed. So trust in Allah and hope in Him, for the afflicted is he who is deprived of reward. Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"2889","Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Hafs Amr b. Ali narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shayban b. Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: from Jabir, from Abu Jafar Muhammad b. Ali b. Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined three things at his death: he enjoined that the army of Usamah be dispatched, and that none should dwell with him in Madinah except the people of his religion. Muhammad said: And I forgot the third."
"2890","Ahmad b. Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Hafs b. Umar al-Mazini narrated to us: Artah b. al-Ashath al-Adawi narrated to us: Bishr b. Abdullah b. Amr b. Said al-Khathami narrated to us, who said: I entered upon Muhammad b. Ali b. Husayn while his son was with him. He said: Come to lunch. I said: I have already lunched, O son of the Messenger of Allah. He said to me: It is endive. I said: O son of the Messenger of Allah, what is in endive? He said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no leaf of endive but upon it is a drop of the water of Paradise. Then oil was brought, and he said: Anoint yourself. I said: I have already anointed myself, O son of the Messenger of Allah. He said: It is violet oil. I said: And what is in violet oil? He said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The superiority of violet oil over all other oils is like the superiority of the offspring of Abd al-Muttalib over all Quraysh, and the superiority of violet oil is like the superiority of Islam over all other religions."
"2891","Fatimah bt. al-Husayn from her father, may Allah be pleased with her: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Kathir narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Musab b. Muhammad narrated to me: from Yala b. Abi Yahya, from Fatimah bt. al-Husayn, from her father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beggar has a right even if he comes on a horse."
"2892","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Qanabi narrated to us: Khalid b. Ilyas narrated to us: from Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Amr b. Uthman, from Fatimah bt. al-Husayn, from Husayn b. Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves noble and lofty matters and dislikes their trifles."
"2893","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl b. al-Hubab al-Jumahi and Ibrahim b. Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us; they said: Abd al-Rahman b. Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us: Hisham Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us: from his mother Fatimah bt. al-Husayn, from her father, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is struck by a calamity and says when he remembers it: {To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return}, Allah renews for him a reward like what it was on the day it struck him."
"2894","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Musa b. Abd al-Rahman al-Bakri narrated to us: Uthman b. Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi narrated to us: Aishah bt. Talhah narrated to us: from Fatimah bt. al-Husayn, from her father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not disturb birds in their nests, for the night is a security for them."
"2895","Al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: from al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: from his mother Fatimah bt. al-Husayn, from her father al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not gaze continuously at lepers."
"2896","Yahya b. Abd al-Baqi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid b. Sulayman narrated to us: from Umarah b. Ghaziyyah, from Fatimah bt. al-Husayn, from her father: that Abdullah b. Amr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it pride to wear a fine suit? He said: No. He said: Is it pride to ride a noble camel? He said: No. He said: Is it pride to prepare food, invite people to eat with me, and have them walk behind me? He said: No. He said: What then is pride? He said: To despise truth and to belittle people."
"2897","Sukaynah bt. al-Husayn from her father: Masadah b. Sad al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us: Ibrahim b. al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ibrahim, freedman of Jumay b. Harithah al-Ansari, narrated to us: Abdullah b. Mahan al-Azdi narrated to me: Fayid, freedman of Ubaydullah b. Abi Rafi, narrated to me: Sukaynah bt. al-Husayn b. Ali narrated to me: from her father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The bearers of the Quran are the nobles of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection."
"2898","Ubaydullah b. Abi Yazid from al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them: Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Amr b. Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, who said: I asked Ubaydullah b. Abi Yazid: Did you see al-Husayn b. Ali? He said: Yes, I saw him sitting in the basin of Zamzam. I said: Did you see him dye? He said: No, except that I saw him with his beard black up to this place - meaning his tuft - with whiteness below that. And he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had grayed in that place of his, and he used to imitate him."
"2899","Ubaydullah b. al-Harith from al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us: from Jabir, from Amr b. Khubayb, from Ubaydullah b. al-Hurr: that he asked al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrust to you anything concerning this march of yours? He said: No."
"2900","Al-Muttalib b. Abdullah b. al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him: Ali b. Said al-Razi narrated to us: Yaqub b. Humayd narrated to us: Sufyan b. Hamzah narrated to us: from Kathir b. Zayd, from al-Muttalib b. Abdullah, who said: When al-Husayn b. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was surrounded, he said: What is the name of this place? They said: Karbala. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth; it is grief and tribulation."
"2901","Talha ibn Ubaydillah from al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Sufi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Talha ibn Ubaydillah, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: What a fine thing is a gift before a need."
"2902","Bishr ibn Ghalib from al-Husayn ibn Ali: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, (ha). And Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, both said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir, from Bishr ibn Ghalib, from Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking while standing."
"2903","Al-Bahzi from al-Husayn: Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, (ha). And al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ata, from al-Bahzi, he said: I asked al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the tashahhud of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: It is the tashahhud of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: And the tashahhud of Abdullah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved to make things light for his ummah. I said: How did Ali say the tashahhud of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good, continual, pure, wholesome words belong to Allah."
"2904","Abu Sa'id al-Taymi Aqisa from al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Abu Sa'id al-Taymi, he said: I heard al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears a notorious garment among clothes, Allah will turn away from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"2905","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir, from Abu Sa'id al-Taymi, from al-Hasan and al-Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2906","Sinan ibn Abi Sinan from al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan, that he heard Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hid smoke for Ibn Said, then asked him what he had hidden for him, and he said: Dukh. He said: Be gone, for you will never go beyond your measure. When he turned away, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did he say? Some said: Dukh, and some said: Rather he said: Zukh. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have differed while I am among you, so after me you will differ even more."
"2907","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he hid smoke for Ibn Said, asked him what he had hidden for him, and he said: Dukh. He said: Be gone, for you will never go beyond your term. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away, the people said: What did he say? Some said: Dukh, and some said: Rather Zukh. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This while you are with me you differ, so after me you will differ even more."
"2908","Abayah ibn Rifah from al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Abayah ibn Rifah, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am cowardly and I am weak. He said: Come to a jihad in which there is no thorn: Hajj."
"2909","Habib ibn Abi Thabit from al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Amr ibn Thabit informed us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, he said: A woman of the women of al-Husayn made food on some of his land, then he ate and the food was lifted, then a freedman of his came, and he called for the food, and he said: O Abu Abdillah, I do not want it. He said: Why? He said: We ate just now with Ubaydullah ibn Abbas. Then al-Husayn said: His father was the chief of Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, feed food and speak good words."
"2910","Abu Hazim al-Ashjai from al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Salim, meaning Ibn Abi Hafsah, from Abu Hazim, he said: I witnessed Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, when al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, died, while he was pushing on the neck of Sa'id ibn al-As, saying: Step forward, for were it not that it is the Sunnah - meaning the gray-haired - I would not have put you forward. And Sa'id was governor over Madinah that day."
"2911","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Husayn al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Sufyan, from Salim ibn Abi Hafsah, from Abu Hazim, he said: I saw al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, put Sa'id ibn al-As forward at the funeral of al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2912","Chapter: those named Hamzah. 237 - Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf, uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The mother of Hamzah: Halah bint Uhayb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah. He witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his kunyah was Abu Umarah, and it is said: Abu Yala. Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Jawaribi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi, from Abi Awn, freedman of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Ibn Abbas, from his father, he said: Abd al-Muttalib married Halah bint Uhayb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah, and she bore him Hamzah and Safiyyah."
"2913","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abi al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib."
"2914","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf."
"2915","Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to me, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Jawaribi al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi, from Abi Awn, freedman of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from al-Miswar, from Ibn Abbas, from his father, he said: Abd al-Muttalib said: I went out to Yemen on one of the two winter-summer journeys, and I stayed with a Jewish man, then a man of the monastery folk saw me, asked my lineage and I gave it to him. He said: Do you permit me to look at part of you? I said: Yes, so long as it is not private. He opened one of my nostrils and looked, then looked in the other, and said: I bear witness that in one of your hands is kingship and in the other prophethood, and we find that among Banu Zuhrah, so how is that? I said: I do not know. He said: Do you have a shaah? I said: What is shaah? He said: A wife. I said: As of today, no. He said: When you return, marry among Banu Zuhrah. So Abd al-Muttalib returned and married Halah bint Wuhayb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah, and she bore him Hamzah and Safiyyah, and he married his son Abdullah to Aminah bint Wahb, and Quraysh said: Abd al-Muttalib has outdone his son. She bore him the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him, was the milk-brother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Thuwaybah, freedwoman of Abu Lahab, suckled them both, and he was older than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2916","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I not point you to the finest young woman of Quraysh? He said: Who is she? He said: The daughter of Hamzah. He said: She is the daughter of my milk-brother."
"2917","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both said: Musaddad narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, will you have your uncle's daughter, the most beautiful young woman in Quraysh? He said: Do you not know that Hamzah is my brother through suckling?"
"2918","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abi Awn, from Abi Salih al-Hanafi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to marry her, and he said: She is the daughter of my brother through suckling."
"2919","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you avoiding Quraysh and leaving us? He said: Do you have something? I said: Yes, the daughter of Hamzah. He said: She is the daughter of my brother through suckling."
"2920","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was propositioned regarding the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and what is forbidden by lineage is forbidden by suckling."
"2921","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was propositioned regarding the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, makes forbidden through suckling what He makes forbidden through lineage."
"2922","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Muslim saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Muslim saying: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman saying: I heard Umm Salamah saying: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, where are you regarding the daughter of Hamzah? Or it was said: Will you not propose to the daughter of Hamzah? He said: Hamzah is my brother through suckling."
"2923","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi informed me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi saying: The Islam of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may Allah have mercy on him, was out of protective zeal. He was a man who shot arrows, and he used to go out of the Sanctuary hunting, and when he returned he passed by the gathering of Quraysh, who used to sit at al-Safa and al-Marwah, and he would pass by them saying: I shot such-and-such, and did such-and-such, then he would go to his house. One day he came from his shooting, and a woman met him and said: O Abu Umarah, what did your brother's son meet from Abu Jahl ibn Hisham? He seized him and did to him and did. He said: Did anyone see him? She said: Yes, by Allah, people saw him. So he went until he reached that gathering at al-Safa and al-Marwah, and they were sitting with Abu Jahl among them. He leaned on his bow and said: I shot such-and-such and did such-and-such, then he gripped his hand with the bow and struck with it between the ears of Abu Jahl, breaking its bowstring groove. Then he said: Take it with the bow, and another with the sword. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that he came with the truth from Allah. They said: O Abu Umarah, he reviled our gods; had it been you, and you are better than him, we would not have approved you for that, and you were never obscene, O Abu Umarah."
"2924","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yaqub al-Juzajani narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yaqub ibn Utbah ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas ibn Shariq, ally of Banu Zuhrah, that Abu Jahl intercepted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Safa and harmed him. Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him, was a man of hunting, and that day he was on his hunt. When he returned, his wife, who had seen what Abu Jahl did to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said to him: O Abu Umarah, had you seen what he did - meaning Abu Jahl - to your brother's son? So Hamzah became angry and went as he was before entering his house, with his bow hanging on his neck, until he entered the mosque. He found Abu Jahl in a gathering of Quraysh, and did not speak to him until he struck his head with his bow and wounded it. Men of Quraysh rose to Hamzah to hold him back from him, and Hamzah said: My religion is the religion of Muhammad. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah. By Allah, I will not turn back from that, so prevent me from that if you are truthful. When Hamzah became Muslim, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Muslims were strengthened by him, some of their affair was established, Quraysh feared him, and they knew that Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him, would protect him."
"2925","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Hamzah and Zayd ibn Harithah: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that Zayd ibn Harithah said: O Messenger of Allah, you made brotherhood between me and Hamzah."
"2926","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from his father, from Abi Ishaq, from a man of the companions of Ali, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib and Zayd ibn Harithah."
"2927","And Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him, was martyred on the day of Uhud: Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on Friday when he had prayed Friday prayer, and reached the pass of Uhud in the morning, and they met on Saturday in the middle of Shawwal in year three."
"2928","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Uhud was in Shawwal in year three."
"2929","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, regarding the naming of those of the Muslims martyred on the day of Uhud from the Emigrants: Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib."
"2930","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abi Hammad, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered Hamzah he wept, and when he saw his mutilation he sobbed."
"2931","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Sa'id al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Hamzah was struck on the day of Uhud."
"2932","Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Hamzah was struck on the day of Uhud."
"2933","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud, Safiyyah came seeking him, not knowing what had happened to him. She met Ali and al-Zubayr, and Ali said to al-Zubayr: Remind your mother. And al-Zubayr said to Ali: You remind your aunt. She said: What happened to Hamzah? They made her see that they did not know. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: I fear for her mind. So he placed his hand on her chest and supplicated for her, and she said: We belong to Allah and to Him we return, and she wept. Then he came and stood over him while he had been mutilated, and said: Were it not for the grief of women I would have left him until he is gathered from the crops of birds and the bellies of beasts. Then he ordered regarding the slain, and began praying over them, placing nine with Hamzah, saying seven takbirs over them, then they were lifted while Hamzah was left, then he called for nine, and said seven takbirs over them, until he finished with them."
"2934","Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray over the martyrs of Uhud nine with Hamzah as their tenth, until he finished with them."
"2935","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, (ha). And Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, both said: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abi Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud looked at Hamzah killed and mutilated, and saw a sight than which he had never seen one more painful to his heart nor more alarming, and said: May Allah have mercy on you, for you kept ties of kinship and did good deeds, and were it not for the grief of those after you over you, it would please me to leave you until you come in diverse crowds. Then he swore while standing in his place: By Allah, I will mutilate seventy of them in your place. Then the Quran came down while he was standing in his place, not yet having moved: If you punish, then punish with the like of what you were punished with, but if you are patient, it is better for the patient, until the surah was sealed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expiated and refrained from what he had intended."
"2936","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ahmad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, Isa ibn Ubayd al-Kindi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, Abu al-Aliyah narrated to me, from Ubayy ibn Kab, may Allah have mercy on him, he said: On the day of Uhud sixty-four of the Ansar were struck, and six of the Emigrants were struck, among them Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him. They mutilated their slain, and the Ansar said: If we get one day of time against them, we will exceed against them. When the day of the conquest of Makkah came, an unknown man called out: There is no Quraysh after today. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down upon His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If you punish, then punish with the like of what you were punished with, but if you are patient, it is better for the patient. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Refrain from the people."
"2937","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Hamzah after Uhud while he had been mutilated, and said: Were it not that Safiyyah would grieve in herself, I would have left him until the beasts eat him so he is gathered from their bellies. Then he called for a striped cloak, and when it was drawn over his head his feet showed, and when it was drawn over his feet his head showed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Draw it over his head. Clothes were few and the slain many, and one man, two men, and three would be shrouded in one cloth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would ask which of them knew most Quran and put him forward to the qiblah. They were buried and he did not pray over them."
"2938","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Zayd, from Abi Asid al-Sa'idi, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the grave of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. They began dragging the striped cloak over his face, and his feet became uncovered, and dragging it over his feet, and his face became uncovered. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it over his face, and put over his feet some of this foliage. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head, and his companions were weeping. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A time will come upon people when they go out to the countryside, while Madinah is better for them if they knew. None endures its hardship and severity but I will be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"2939","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from his father, (ha). And Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Abi Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Khabbab, he said: I saw Hamzah, and we found for him no cloth to shroud him in except a cloak; when we covered his feet with it his head came out, and when we covered his head with it his feet came out. So we covered his head and placed over his feet some idhkhir."
"2940","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that Hamzah had a striped cloak over him; when his head was covered with it his feet showed, and when his feet were covered his head came out. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding him, so his head was covered and a tree and stones were placed over his feet."
"2941","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zaidah, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded Hamzah in one cloth. Jabir said: That cloth was a striped cloak."
"2942","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned on the day of Uhud and heard the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal weeping over their dead, and said: But Hamzah has no weeping women for him. Then the women of the Ansar came weeping over Hamzah in his presence. He awoke while they were weeping, and said: Woe to them, they are still here until now. Order them to return and not to weep over any dead after today."
"2943","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise last night, and I looked in it, and Hamzah was reclining on a couch."
"2944","Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mansur ibn Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: When Hamzah and his companions were struck on the day of Uhud, they said: Would that those behind us knew what reward Allah gave us, so it would be a reward for them. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I will inform them. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: And do not think those killed in the cause of Allah dead, the verse."
"2945","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Hafs ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, he said: I went out, I and Ubaydullah ibn Adiyy ibn al-Khiyar, and we went to the frontier - meaning the frontier of the Romans - then we passed by Hims, where Wahshi was. I said: If we went to him and asked him about his killing of Hamzah, may Allah have mercy on him, how he killed him? We headed toward him, and a man met us while we were asking about him, and said: He is a man overcome by this wine; if you find him sober you will find him an Arab man who will narrate to you whatever hadith you wish, and if you find him otherwise, then turn away from him. We came to him and found him in his courtyard. He looked at Ubaydullah ibn Adiyy and said: The son of Adiyy ibn al-Khiyar? He said: Yes. He said: I have not seen you since your Sa'di mother handed you to me and no sooner did your feet gleam to me than I knew you. He said: I said to him: We came to you to tell us about your killing of Hamzah, how you killed him? He said: I was a slave of Jubayr ibn Mutim, and his uncle Tuaymah ibn Adiyy had been killed on the day of Badr. He said: If you kill the uncle of Muhammad for my uncle, you are free. So I went out on the day of Uhud among the people with my spear, and my only concern was to be freed. I made Hamzah my business and headed for him, while Siba ibn Abd al-Uzza went before me to him. He said: I turned from him while he was cutting people with his sword, as if he were a dusty-gray camel. When Siba went before me to him, Hamzah said: Come, O son of the cutter of clitorises. He said: He drew near to him and struck him, as if he missed him. I hid behind something and shook my spear until I was satisfied with it, then I threw it, and it fell in his groin. He said: He tried to rise and was overcome. I withdrew and returned among the people to Makkah, and was freed. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, I went out to Taif and stayed there. When the people of Taif agreed to make peace with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the ways became straitened for me, and I kept thinking where to go. While I was in my worry, a man met me and said: Why do I see you like this? I said: I did to this man what I did to his uncle, and I see these people have agreed to make peace with him, so I do not know where to go. He said: By Allah, he does not kill anyone who comes to him and bears his testimony. So I went out as I was, and by Allah I did not realize until I stood over his head in Madinah. He raised his head and looked at me and said: Wahshi? I said: Wahshi, and I bore his testimony. He said: Woe to you, tell me about your killing of Hamzah, how you killed him? I told him, by Allah, as I told you both. He said: Woe to you, hide your face from me. I used to avoid him until Allah took him. When Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sent the army to Yamamah, I went out with the people, and I made Musaylimah my business. I charged him, I and a man of the Ansar, with my spear with which I had killed Hamzah. He said: I threw the spear at him, and the Ansari charged him. Your Lord knows best which of us killed him. If I killed him, then I killed the best of people and the worst of people."
"2946","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abi al-Aswad, from Urwah, he said: And killed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud from the Muslims, then from Banu Hashim, Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib; Wahshi, freedman of Utbah ibn Ghazwan, killed him."
"2947","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, he said: I went out, I and Ubaydullah ibn Adiyy ibn al-Khiyar, and we went to the frontier, then we passed by Hims where Wahshi was. He mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Ishaq."
"2948","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Jafar ibn Amr, he said: I went out, I and Ubaydullah ibn Adiyy ibn al-Khiyar, in the time of Muawiyah, and we went to the frontier. When we returned we passed by Hims, where Wahshi ibn Harb was. He mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Ishaq."
"2949","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw in sleep-vision, he said: I saw as if I was riding behind a ram, and as if the tip of my sword broke. I interpreted that I kill the ram of the people, and I interpreted the tip of my sword as the killing of a man of my kin. Then Hamzah was killed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed Talhah, who was the standard-bearer."
"2950","Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it is written with Allah in the seventh heaven: Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib is the Lion of Allah and the Lion of His Messenger."
"2951","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Umayr ibn Ishaq, he said: Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib used to fight before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two swords, saying: I am the Lion of Allah and the Lion of His Messenger."
"2952","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abi Hashim al-Rummani, from Abi Mijlaz, from Qays ibn Abbad, he said: I heard Aba Dharr saying: I swear by Allah, this verse was sent down: These two opponents disputed concerning their Lord, regarding these six: Hamzah, Ubaydah, and Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with them, and Utbah, Shaybah sons of Rabiah, and al-Walid ibn Utbah. They had dueled on the day of Badr."
"2953","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I, Hamzah, and Ubaydah ibn al-Harith were helped on the day of Badr against al-Walid ibn Utbah - I think he said: That was not hidden from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2954","Mahmud al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us, Rahmah ibn Musab al-Bahili narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, he said: A man called Hawdhah came to Muawiyah, and Muawiyah said to him: O Hawdhah, did you witness Badr? He said: Yes, Commander of the Faithful, against me not for me. He said: How long ago for you? He said: I was that day firm and strong like a smooth hard rock, as if I see them lined for us in a long line, and as if I see the gleam of their swords like sun rays through clouds. I did not wake until the attackers of the people overwhelmed us, at their front Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, a fierce lion tearing utterly, saying: You will never eat dates in the belly of Makkah, you will never eat dates in the belly of Makkah. Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib followed him, with a white feather on his chest by which he was marked, as if he were a camel crushing dry stalks. I feared them both, and they turned upon Hanzalah - meaning the brother of Muawiyah. Then Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Aside from you, and no ingratitude to Allah, you kept on; would that I knew when you rested, O Hawdhah? He said: By Allah, Commander of the Faithful, I did not rest until I looked at the hills of Arthad. I said: Would that I knew what Hanzalah did. Then Muawiyah said: Your mentioning Hanzalah is like the rich mentioning his poor brother, for he hardly mentions except drowsy or feigning sleep."
"2955","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, Musa ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from his father, he said: Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib on the day of Badr was marked with an ostrich feather. A man of the polytheists said: Who is the man marked with an ostrich feather? It was said: Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. He said: That is the one who did to us what he did."
"2956","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Usamah al-Kalbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Ali ibn al-Hazawwar, al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The master of martyrs is Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib."
"2957","What Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him, transmitted with chain: Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Khallad al-Bahili and Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, both said: Salma ibn Iyad ibn Munqidh ibn Salma ibn Malik narrated to us, my grandfather Munqidh ibn Salma narrated to me, from the hadith of his grandfather Malik, from the hadith of his grandfather Abi Marthad, from the hadith of his ally Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib - and he was his ally since no servant coaxed a milch-camel, no boy called his father, and no one stayed in his place - he narrated to him a hadith traced to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Keep to this supplication: O Allah, I ask You by Your Greatest Name, and Your greatest pleasure. Salma says it repeatedly, for it is a name of the names of Allah, Exalted. I never ceased hearing that the forefather of Banu Amir is a rock which water lifts and does not sink. He said: He is Malik son of Fatimah bint Abi Marthad Kinnaz ibn Husayn ibn Nafar ibn Yarbu."
"2958","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Haram ibn Uthman informed me, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came one day to Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib and did not find him. He asked his wife Inabah, who was of Banu al-Najjar, and she said: He went out, may my father be ransom for you, just now heading toward you; I think he missed you in some alley of Banu al-Najjar. Will you not enter, O Messenger of Allah? So he entered, and she served him hays, and he ate of it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, with enjoyment and wholesomeness, you have come while I wanted to come to you to congratulate you. Abu Umarah informed me that you were given a river in Paradise called al-Kawthar. He said: Yes, and its courtyard is ruby, coral, peridot, and pearl. She said: I would love for you to describe your Hawd to me with a description I hear from you. He said: It is between Aylah and Sanaa, in it cups like the number of stars, and the most beloved of those who come to it to me are your people, O daughter of Qahd. Meaning the Ansar."
"2959","238 - Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, kunyah Abu Salih, and it is said: Abu Muhammad: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Khallad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him the kunyah Abu Salih."
"2960","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from Hamzah ibn Amr: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am a man who fasts continuously, shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2961","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from Hamzah al-Aslami, that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am a man who fasts, shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2962","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Malik informed us, (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I fast while traveling? He fasted much, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2963","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Aishah, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2964","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2965","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, he said: Urwah informed me, from Aishah, that Hamzah al-Aslami came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who used to travel, shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2966","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Aishah informed him that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I am a man who fasts while traveling? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2967","Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am a man who fasts, shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2968","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who fasts continuously, shall I fast while traveling? He said: Fast if you wish, and break fast if you wish."
"2969","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2970","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mutamir narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2971","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that Hamzah al-Aslami said: O Messenger of Allah, I have strength while traveling, shall I fast? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2972","Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah - a man of Aslam - said: O Messenger of Allah, I fast continuously and do not break fast, shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2973","Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2974","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, my father narrated to me, from Aishah, that Hamzah ibn Amr said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to fast continuously, shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2975","Abd al-Kabir ibn Umar al-Khattabi narrated to us, Umar ibn Mudrik al-Razi narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2976","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Barrad al-Ashari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hamzah ibn Amr, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2977","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah informed us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, he said: I said: O Messenger, I am strong for fasting. He said: If you are strong, then you and that."
"2978","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Attar al-Habhabi narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: Fast if you wish, and break fast if you wish."
"2979","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Abi al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Abi Murawih, from Hamzah al-Aslami, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have strength for fasting while traveling, is there any sin upon me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a concession from Allah, Mighty and Majestic; whoever wishes takes it, then it is good, and whoever loves to fast, there is no sin upon him."
"2980","Sulayman ibn Yasar from Hamzah: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2981","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Hamzah al-Aslami, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: You have the choice; if you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2982","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Hamzah al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, you fasted, and if you wish, you broke fast."
"2983","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, (ha). And Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, both said: al-Layth narrated to us, (ha). And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Hamzah al-Aslami said: O Messenger of Allah, I find strength for fasting while traveling. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2984","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Hamzah al-Aslami, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"2985","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Hamzah al-Aslami, that he saw a man at Mina circumambulating on his reddish camel saying: Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among them."
"2986","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Hamzah ibn Amr: Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abi Salamah, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he said: Whichever is easier for you, do it."
"2987","Al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Rashid al-Nasri narrated to us, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Aslamis: Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I am with Mihjan ibn al-Adra. The people held back. He said: What is with you? They said: Whomever you are with has won. He said: Then shoot, and I am with all of you."
"2988","Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami from his father: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, (ha). And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, (ha). And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, all said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hizami narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, that Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami informed him, that his father informed him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put him in command of a detachment. He said: I went out in it, and he said: If you seize so-and-so, burn him with fire. When I turned, he called me and said: If you seize him, kill him, for none punishes with fire except the Lord of fire. The wording is of the hadith of Sa'id ibn Mansur."
"2989","Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, from his father, he said: We were mustered while on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a dark slippery night, and my fingers lit up until they gathered upon them their camels and what had fallen of their goods, and my fingers indeed shone."
"2990","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Hamzah narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hamzah ibn Malik ibn Hamzah al-Madini narrated to us, my uncle Sufyan ibn Hamzah narrated to me, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, from his father Hamzah ibn Amr, he said: The food of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to rotate among his companions, this one night and this one night. He said: It came to me one night, so I made the food of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), left the skin and did not tie it, and went with the food to him. It moved and what was in it spilled. I said: Upon my hand is spilled the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring it near. I said: I cannot, O Messenger of Allah. I returned to my place, and the skin was saying: Qab qab. I said: Hush, a remainder had spilled that remained in it. I came to look in it and found it filled to its breasts. I pulled it and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Indeed, had you left it, it would have filled to its mouth, then been tied."
"2991","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Yahya ibn Yazid Abu Khalid al-Khuzai narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the expedition of Tabuk, and I was in his service that journey. I looked at the ghee-skin and little remained in it. I prepared food for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), placed the skin in the sun, and slept. I awoke to the gurgling of the skin. I stood and took its head with my hand. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me and said: Had you left it, it would have flowed a valley of ghee."
"2992","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, that Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami narrated to him, that he heard his father Hamzah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the back of every camel is a devil, so when you ride them, mention Allah, then do not fall short of your need."
"2993","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Majid al-Madani narrated to us, he said: I heard Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami mentioning that his father informed him, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man of camels, I manage them, travel upon them and hire them out, and this month - meaning Ramadan - sometimes meets me while I find strength, and I am wintering; I find fasting, O Messenger of Allah, easier for me than delaying it so it becomes a debt upon me. Shall I fast, O Messenger of Allah, greater for my reward, or break fast? He said: Whichever you wish, O Hamzah."
"2994","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abi al-Zinad, Hanzalah al-Aslami informed me, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and a group with him as a detachment to a man of his enemy, saying: If you overpower so-and-so, burn him with fire. They went until, when they had disappeared from him, he called them and sent after them and brought them back. Then he said: If you overpower him, kill him, and do not burn him with fire, for none punishes with fire except the Lord of fire."
"2995","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, (ha). And Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Salim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abi al-Ashath al-Attar, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, he said: I asked him about fasting while traveling. He said: We used to fast and break fast, and the breaker did not blame the faster, nor the faster the breaker."
"2996","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hamzah ibn Amr, he said: I ate food with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Eat with your right, eat from what is near you, and mention the name of Allah."
"2997","Al-Hadrami said: I heard Minjab ibn al-Harith saying: This is a mistake which Sharik made. Ali ibn Mushir informed us of it, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. Hamzah ibn Amr, and it is not sound; Sharik erred in it."
"2998","239 - Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, kunyah Abu Abdillah, al-Absi: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Aqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Jami al-Arhabi, he said: I came, I and a companion of mine, to Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, and we said: O Abu Abdillah."
"2999","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adiyy narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, that Hudhayfah was one of Banu Abs, and his number was among the Ansar."
"3000","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abi Ishaq, from Musab ibn Sad, he said: The polytheists seized Hudhayfah and his father before Badr, wanted to kill them, and took upon them a covenant and pledge not to aid against them. They released them both, and they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We gave them that we will not aid against them; if you wish, we will fight with you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather we fulfill for them, and we seek Allah's help against them."
